{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C8fFet9nntynbPT63qJaWS","type":"tool_result","content":"# Working in this repo\n\n## Finish every change on main\n\n- When a `/goal` is complete, or a prompt has changed the repo, commit and\n  push to `origin/main` right away.\n- Pushing does not deploy. Vercel usage costs too much to build every\n  change, so Git deploys are off (`\"git\": { \"deploymentEnabled\": false }`\n  in `vercel.json`) and the site runs locally: `pnpm dev`, then\n  http://127.0.0.1:7417. Deploy to Vercel only when Michael explicitly asks,\n  for a major update: push with `deploymentEnabled` set to `true` (that push\n  deploys; check it reaches READY), then set it back to `false` in the next\n  commit, which does not deploy.\n- Work on `main`. If a branch is ever needed, merge it into main and delete\n  it (locally and on GitHub) in the same session. Never leave a local\n  branch, an unpushed commit, a stash, or an open PR behind.\n- Before starting work, run `git fetch --prune` and look at\n  `gh pr list`. Anything open gets resolved first.\n\n## Pull requests from others\n\nDecide each one; do not let it sit. Accept it (merge to main, delete the\nbranch), reject it (close it with a one-line reason), or replace it (close\nit, and land a better version on main that says which PR it replaces).\n\n## Keep it simple and clean\n\n- No dependencies, no build step, no generated files committed\n  (`data/games.json` is gitignored and rebuilt by `scripts/scan.mjs`).\n- Run `pnpm test` (or `node --test \"scripts/**/*.test.mjs\"`) before\n  committing code.\n- Delete what is no longer used instead of leaving it around.\n\n## When something goes wrong\n\nRoll back rather than leave half-finished work. Revert the commit\n(`git revert`) or restore the last good state and push that, so main is\nalways a working wall. Say what was rolled back and why.\n======\n116:A folder under `games/` is one of three things, decided by what is in it:\n164:  folder. A zip of several single-file games becomes a collection. A package\n200:**Local engine dependencies.** The importer also recognizes Three.js and\n203:HTML and separate JavaScript modules, adds the import maps needed by addons,\n205:`three` and `@dimforge/rapier…` imports use the game's detected version, or the\n208:are preserved. Games copied by hand must supply their own correct import map;\n211:The shelf includes all 13 Three.js releases from `0.180.0` through `0.186.1`\n214:See `lib/vendor/README.md` for paths, import maps and verification commands.\n216:**Size.** GitHub refuses any single file over 100 MB and warns above 50 MB;\n238:The first reads every game in full, about half a minute at two thousand games;\n260:The bar in the corner has three buttons: **←** back to the wall, **🎲** roll\n309:cabinet with its whole blurb beside the screen) or *Three per row*. A phone\n341:- **How a session works**, in three steps, and the **ways to win**.\n348:  many games it leaves. A browser with no WebGPU is told how many of them need\n363:each series with three or more games (*Inspired by Final Fantasy*) and each\n364:model that made three or more, *Originals*, *Couch co-op* (several players on\n453:All three include text search, Games / All entries / Tech demos & tools /\n464:Every game can be played with up to three friends, each on their own device,\n475:way to build the game. A game declares one of three modes:\n498:(`1–4 players · Parallel · about 4 min`), and the Catalogue finds them all\n520:and is never dealt. The three examples in `lib/hub/examples/` (**Starfall**,\n542:node scripts/retrofit.mjs pick --wave 1 > .cache/wave1.txt   # one build of each title: readable, no WebGPU needed; smallest first\n543:awk 'NR % 7 == 0' .cache/wave1.txt > .cache/pilot.txt        # a pilot of about thirty, small to large\n552:  (`hub-check --draws-only`), and spends nothing on one it can't: a WebGPU-only\n553:  game in a browser without WebGPU, even when its title screen shows. On a\n572:one. Run a pilot of about thirty varied games, read the pass rate and cost per\n574:for you: commit what passed in batches of about fifty.\n579:the host picks how to win (**Party**: 8 rounds and three bonus awards worth 3\n605:about half a minute from one game to the next, less when everyone is ready\n688:  works as before. The free project pauses after about a week without use;\n842:  check3d.py      one 3D game in headless browsers, WebGL2 and WebGPU\n846:  three/          three.js r186, the one copy every 3D game imports\n850:  vendor/         versioned Three.js and Rapier packages for imported games\n853:The games on the shared kit run on the same stack: three.js r186 with `WebGPURenderer`\n854:(WebGL2 when WebGPU is missing), loaded once from `lib/three` through an\n855:import map, and the kit in `lib/kit` for boot, quality tiers and keyboard,\n858:upgrading three.js and Rapier and the local patches to re-apply.\n868:library shelf cut to the files games actually load (about 14,700 files in all,\n894:in the review search. **Reset audio filters** clears all three controls.\n======\ndocs/curation-2026-09-24.md\ndocs/curation-2026-09-28-new-ai-stuff.md\ndocs/curation-2026-09-28.md\ndocs/curation-2026-10-28.md\ndocs/import-registry.md\ndocs/multiplayer-plan.md\ndocs/session-hub.md\n\ndocs:\ncuration-2026-09-24.md\ncuration-2026-09-28-new-ai-stuff.md\ncuration-2026-09-28.md\ncuration-2026-10-28.md\nimport-registry.md\nimports\nmultiplayer-plan.md\nsession-hub.md\nsuperpowers\n\ndocs/imports:\n2026-10-13-baseline-tests.txt\n2026-10-13-browser-checks.json\n2026-10-13-cinder-choir-and-threads-sites.md\n2026-10-13-drive-games.json\n2026-10-13-drive-games.md\n2026-10-13-final-tests.txt\n2026-10-13-github-audit.json\n2026-10-13-github-browser-checks.json\n2026-10-13-github-build-fingerprints.json\n2026-10-13-github-builds.json\n2026-10-13-github-corrected-dry-run.json\n2026-10-13-github-five-audit.json\n2026-10-13-github-five-games.md\n2026-10-