{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016PVtSMCoQt7FetJY3L7JFu","type":"tool_result","content":"<!DOCTYPE html>\n<!--\n  my-3D2dge (My \"3D\" 2D Game Engine), {{EDITION}} v{{VERSION}} ({{BUILD}})\n  https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\n\n  AI MODELS: this one file is the engine, the 3D engine, their documentation and {{GAMES}}.\n    1. Read the 3D engine's manual: the comment at the top of the script marked \"inlined from engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js\".\n       Then the API card in <script type=\"text/markdown\" id=\"my3d2dge-api\"> below, for what the 2D engine still does in\n       a 3D game: the game and its scenes, input, the rigs and their moves, the HUD (font, ui, menus), sound.\n    2. The engines are the scripts marked \"inlined from engine/...\". They are yours to change: fix, extend or rewrite\n       any of them as you see fit (their sources, readable, are in the repository's engine/).{{ENGINE}}\n    3. The games live between GAME START and GAME END: {{CONTENTS}}\n       To make a new game, change the slice closest to your genre into yours (its own title, play and game-over\n       scenes) and delete what you don't use of the rest.\n    4. SERVED, NOT DOUBLE-CLICKED: the 3D engine loads three.js r182 and Rapier 0.19.3 from /vendor/ (this repository's\n       vendor/ folder) through the import map below. Serve the repository's root (npx serve, python3 -m http.server)\n       and open this file there, or open it on my-3d2dge.vercel.app. Elsewhere, copy vendor/ beside it and change the\n       four \"/vendor/\" paths to \"./vendor/\".\n  HUMANS: open it served and play. Press ? for the API card.\n  {{LINKS}}\n-->\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\">\n<title>my-3D2dge · {{EDITION}}</title>\n<script type=\"text/markdown\" id=\"my3d2dge-api\">\n<!-- @inline-raw API.md -->\n</script>\n<script type=\"importmap\">\n{\n  \"imports\": {\n    \"three\": \"/vendor/three-0.182.0/three.webgpu.min.js\",\n    \"three/webgpu\": \"/vendor/three-0.182.0/three.webgpu.min.js\",\n    \"three/tsl\": \"/vendor/three-0.182.0/three.tsl.min.js\",\n    \"@dimforge/rapier3d-simd-compat\": \"/vendor/rapier3d-simd-compat-0.19.3/rapier.js\"\n  }\n}\n</script>\n<style>\nhtml,body{margin:0;height:100%;background:#000;overflow:hidden;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;-webkit-tap-highlight-color:transparent}\n#stage{position:relative;width:100%;height:100%;overflow:hidden;background:#000;touch-action:none}\n#view{position:absolute;left:0;top:0;display:block;pointer-events:none;z-index:0}\n#screen{position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;display:block;image-rendering:pixelated;z-index:1;background:transparent}\n#guideBtn{position:absolute;top:calc(8px + env(safe-area-inset-top,0px));right:calc(112px + env(safe-area-inset-right,0px));z-index:5;font:600 12px/1 ui-monospace,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#d8d0f0;background:rgba(20,16,40,.6);border:1px solid rgba(216,208,240,.3);border-radius:4px;padding:5px 7\n#guideBtn:hover,#guideBtn:focus-visible{opacity:1}\n#guideBtn.away{opacity:0;transition:opacity .4s;pointer-events:none}\n@media (pointer:coarse){#guideBtn{display:none}}\n#guide{position:absolute;inset:0;z-index:6;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;padding:16px;background:rgba(0,0,0,.6)}\n#guide[hidden]{display:none}\n#guide .panel{width:min(860px,100%);max-height:100%;display:flex;flex-direction:column;background:#141226;color:#eee8ff;border:1px solid #4a4470;border-radius:6px}\n#guide header{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;padding:10px 14px;border-bottom:1px solid #4a4470;font:600 14px system-ui,sans-serif}\n#guide header button{font:inherit;color:inherit;background:#2a2648;border:1px solid #4a4470;border-radius:4px;padding:5px 10px;cursor:pointer}\n#guide pre{margin:0;padding:14px;overflow:auto;font:12.5px/1.5 ui-monospace