lcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\n\n  AI MODELS: this one file is the engine, the 3D engine, their documentation and {{GAMES}}.\n    1. Read the 3D engine's manual: the comment at the top of the script marked \"inlined from engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js\".\n       Then the API card in <script type=\"text/markdown\" id=\"my3d2dge-api\"> below, for what the 2D engine still does in\n       a 3D game: the game and its scenes, input, the rigs and their moves, the HUD (font, ui, menus), sound.\n    2. The engines are the scripts marked \"inlined from engine/...\". They are yours to change: fix, extend or rewrite\n       any of them as you see fit (their sources, readable, are in the repository's engine/).{{ENGINE}}\n    3. The games live between GAME START and GAME END: {{CONTENTS}}\n       To make a new game, change the slice closest to your genre into yours (its own title, play and game-over\n       scenes) and delete what you don't use of the rest.\n    4. SERVED, NOT DOUBLE-CLICKED: the 3D engine loads three.js r182 and Rapier 0.19.3 from /vendor/ (this repository's\n       vendor/ folder) through the import map below. Serve the repository's root (npx serve, python3 -m http.server)\n       and open this file there, or open it on my-3d2dge.vercel.app. Elsewhere, copy vendor/ beside it and change the\n       four \"/vendor/\" paths to \"./vendor/\".\n  HUMANS: open it served and play. Press ? for the API card.\n  {{LINKS}}\n-->\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\">\n<title>my-3D2dge · {{EDITION}}</title>\n<script type=\"text/markdown\" id=\"my3d2dge-api\">\n<!-- @inline-raw API.md -->\n</script>\n<script type=\"importmap\">\n{\n  \"imports\": {\n    \"three\": \"/vendor/three-0.182.0/three.webgpu.min.js\",\n    \"three/webgpu\": \"/vendor/three-0.182.0/three.webgpu.min.js\",\n    \"three/tsl\": \"/vendor/three-0.182.0/three.tsl.min.js\",\n    \"@dimforge/rapier3d-simd-