{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ND1dWwzsrjDc2BXWgGMrdy","type":"tool_result","content":"API-INDEX.md:91:- 1234 Module arcade: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode (engine/modules/arcade.js); E.Arcade: arcade\nAPI-INDEX.md:492:- `game.hook(kind, fn)` †: a function of the game's own on the engine's clock: kind 'input' fn(dt) every step, paused or not, after the input is read (a host's guard, an idle timer); 'step' fn(dt) every update step in play, before the scene's update (an attract mode's watcher); 'ent\nAPI-INDEX.md:505:- `game.script(fn, o)` †: run a coroutine on game time, in the update step: game.script(function* (game) { yield .5; yield E.until(() => door.open); yield game.tween(cam, { y: 0 }, 1); yield E.all([a, b]); ... }, { keep }). Each yield waits: a number (seconds), nothing (one step), a\nAPI-INDEX.md:1234:## Module arcade: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode (engine/modules/arcade.js)\nAPI-INDEX.md:1236:- `new E.Arcade(game, o = {}) → arcade`: new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [] (the scores that give a life) or every (a life each that many points), credits: null (free play) or the coins a game takes, idle: 20, demo: 30, scores: 6 (the attract mode's seconds), hud: true, c\nAPI-INDEX.md:1238:- `arcade.attract(dt)`: the attract mode, each step on the title: 'title', 'demo' (o.idle seconds without input; it lasts o.demo seconds or until endDemo()), 'scores' (o.scores seconds), then 'title' again; any input goes back to 'title'\nAPI-INDEX.md:1247:- `arcade.drawTable(r, mode = '', y = 40, title = 'HIGH SCORES')`: a table as a screen (the attract mode's, or after a game), its title at y: rank, name, score\nAPI-INDEX.md:1248:- `arcade.endDemo()`: the demo is over (a demo in a scene of its own: call it on the way back): the attract mode shows the scores\nAPI-INDEX.md:1252:- `arcade.start(players = 1, o = {})`: begin a game for 1 or 2 players (taking turns), o: { demo: true } for the attract mode's; spends the credits a game takes unless it is free play or a demo. Returns false without them\nAPI-INDEX.md:1255:- `arcade.wake()`: the attract mode back to the title, its idle clock at zero (as any input does)\nAPI-INDEX.md:1265:- `arcade.phase = 'title'`: the attract mode's, 'title' | 'demo' | 'scores'\nAI_GUIDE.md:364:- **The modules:** `grid` (square and hex grids: A* paths, move ranges with climb and drop past allies, lines, symmetric fields of view, `E.Fog`, flood fills and groups, tactics' shapes of effect, facing and threat maps, `E.GridMover` for Pac-Man's and Sokoban's moves, `E.Turns` by s\nAI_GUIDE.md:452:- `new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [10000] })` keeps the score, lives, two players' turns (each one's stage in `p.save`), the continue, the tables with initials and the attract mode; `cab.update(dt)` each step and `cab.draw(r, box)` after the game.\nAI_GUIDE.md:627:  - An autopilot drives the hero through a virtual input for balance runs and an attract-mode demo.\n\n==== never\n987:    if (this._never) { this.touchEnabled = false; if (this.stickOn) this._stickEnd({ pointerId: this.stickId }); return null; }   // (touch: 'never')\n2420:    if ((this.input._never = this.o.touch === 'never')) this.input.touchEnabled = false;   // (a game that never shows touch controls)\n2577:    if (this.o.touch === 'never') on(window, 'keydown', () => { this._keyed = true; });   // (a keyboard is there: the notice below goes)\n2617:    if (this.o.touch === 'never' && this._needSync) this._needSync();   // (section 10l)\n3104:    for (const k in STANDARD_SETTINGS) if (!(game.o.touch === 'never' && STANDARD_SETTINGS[k].group === 'Touch')) this.define(Object.assign({ key: k }, STANDARD_SETTINGS[k]));   // (touch: 'never': no Touch group)\n3989: *    game's own function on the engine's clock), and the notice a game made with touch: 'never' shows on a phone. In a\n4015:/** touch: 'never' on a device with touch alone: \"Controller or keyboard required\", with Settings, until a controller\n\n==== STANDARD_SETTINGS\n2523:  _zoomStd() { const sp = this.settings && this.settings.spec('zoom'); return !!sp && sp.apply === STANDARD_SETTINGS.zoom.apply; }\n3045:const STANDARD_SETTINGS = {\n3090:   * beside the standard ones (STANDARD_SETTINGS). Saved with E.store under 'settings:' + the game's id, with a version;\n3104:    for (const k in STANDARD_SETTINGS) if (!(game.o.touch === 'never' && STANDARD_SETTINGS[k].group === 'Touch')) this.define(Object.assign({ key: k }, STANDARD_SETTINGS[k]));   // (touch: 'never\n3105:    for (const sp of own) this.define(sp && !sp.label && Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(STANDARD_SETTINGS, sp.key) ? Object.assign({ key: sp.key }, STANDARD_SETTINGS[sp.key], sp) : sp);   /\n9495:  _items() { const it = this._o.settings && this._o.settings.items || []; return it.map(i => typeof i === 'string' ? Object.assign({ key: i }, STANDARD_SETTINGS[i]) : i).filter(i => i && i.key); \n3024: *      one with a standard key and no label changes that setting, its other fields kept: { key: 'glyphs', value:\n3054:  music: { group: 'Sound', label: 'Music', type: 'slider', value: .5, apply: (g, v) => { g.audio.musicVolume = v; g.audio.applyVolume(); } },\n7680:     *  is none); volume: master volume 0..1; sfxVolume, musicVolume, voiceVolume: 0..1 for effects, music and the voice\n7682:    this._game = game; this._signal = signal; this.ctx = null; this.volume = .7; this.sfxVolume = 1; this.musicVolume = .5; this.voiceVolume = 1; this.muted = false;\n7715:  /** apply volume, musicVolume, sfxVolume and mute after setting them directly (setVolume and mute call it) */\n7716:  applyVolume() { if (!this.ctx) return; this._master.gain.value = this.muted ? 0 : this.volume; this._sfxBus.gain.value = this.sfxVolume; this._musBus.gain.value = this.musicVolume * (this._ducked || this.ducked ? .35 : 1); 