{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj9hbsXfbEDTkXwKrPF1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014mDTELEanxL4K47RD46DBg","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"for n in 269 350 492 867 1107 1247 1317 1414 1615 1903 1960 2218 2672 3179 3266; do sed -n \"$((n+1))p\" engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js | cut -c1-150; done; echo; grep -n \"terrain\" engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js | sed -n 1,60p | cut -c1-190","description":"List the 3D engine's section titles and terrain references"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14013,"cache_read_input_tokens":209882,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14013},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ea1b61d-e1b8-4350-be76-ae4a4cbc51a9","uuid":"83cb8bee-81be-4bac-980c-6e40b9a0b089","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:28:59.739Z","request_id":"req_011Cgj9hbd9S3t4FvX7qEYX1","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_014mDTELEanxL4K47RD46DBg":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211923__xa49253/work/.research/engine/my-3d2dge && for n in 269 350 492 867 1107 1247 1317 1414 1615 1903 1960 2218 2672 3179 3266; do sed -n \"$((n+1))p\" engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js | cut -c1-150; done; echo; grep -n \"terrain\" engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js | sed -n 1,60p | cut -c1-190","description":"List the 3D engine's section titles and terrain references"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_014mDTELEanxL4K47RD46DBg":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211923__xa49253/work/.research/engine/my-3d2dge"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014mDTELEanxL4K47RD46DBg","type":"tool_result","content":" * 1. SETUP  units, helpers, collision groups, the page's renderer (World3D.init)\n * 2. TEXTURES AND MATERIALS  everything drawn by code, pixel by pixel, baked into crisp (nearest) textures\n * 3. LEVEL  written as text, one character per floor tile (1 metre, 16 units); row 0 is the far (north) edge, y grows\n * 3b. TERRAIN  an open world instead of a level: new E.World3D(game, { terrain: { size, height, color, ... } })\n * 4. PARTS DRAWN BY CODE  instanced batches of four shapes (tube, ball, box, cone) in a toon look with outlines, and\n * 5. THINGS  pickups and set dressing drawn by code with the pen: world.thing(kind, x, y, z, o). A thing has\n * 5b. SHAPES  the 2D engine's shapes (docs/ASSETS.md: E.SHAPES ids, a store set's 'SET:id', or an entry) in 3D, from the\n * 6. CHARACTERS DRAWN  each rig as it stands (the game poses it; this only reads it), as a Puppet (3D parts on the\n * 7. CAMERA  world.camera: every camera a real 3D one, its pose worked out in the game's fixed steps (so the controls\n * 8. ACTORS  world.hero(o): a kinematic capsule that Rapier's character controller walks (it slides along walls,\n * 8b. VEHICLES AND FLYERS  world.vehicle(o): a kart, a car or a hovercraft, a ball that Rapier rolls (walls, bumps,\n * 9. THE WORLD  new E.World3D(game, o) (after await E.World3D.init(game)): a level, its physics, its actors, props,\n * 10. DRAWING  effects (arcs and rings on the ground, weapon trails, glows, the game's particles), lights (the torches\n * 10b. FILTERS  one look over the finished picture: world.filter = { look, apply, bloom, fxaa, ... } (change it any time)\n * 11. THE ENGINE'S HANDLES  E.World3D (init, the registries, the input preset and settings), E.THREE, E.TSL, E.RAPIER\n\n117:lights: 2 (your own), spots: 0 (flashlights), glowLights: 4, shadows, outlines, filter, camera: { mode, proj, fov, chase, ... }, terrain (an open\n209:## Open worlds: new E.World3D(game, { terrain: { height: (x, y) => z, ... } })\n210:terrain: { size (32768: two kilometres), height, color: (x, y, z, nz, out) => [r, g, b] (0..255), cell (32), chunk (32\n214:and world.terrain.normal(x, y) read the triangles Rapier collides with; flow() goes straight. sky: { top, horizon, ground,\n229:}, track.where(x, y) -> { d, across, z }, track.surface(x, y). A terrain under it keeps below it (your height function).\n868: * 3b. TERRAIN  an open world instead of a level: new E.World3D(game, { terrain: { size, height, color, ... } })\n874: *      queries  world.ground, floorAt, topH (and terrain.normal, slope) read the same triangles Rapier collides with (each\n886:    if (typeof def.height !== 'function') throw new Error('my-3D2dge 3D: a terrain needs height: (x, y) => z, the ground\\'s height in engine units');\n986:/* ---- the terrain's picture: one material (vertex colors, rock strata by height where it is steep, a speckle and a\n1103:/** straight lines over open ground: a terrain's flow field (world.flow()) never steers */\n1661:    /** far: how far it sees (units; a terrain's far); near: its near plane (units; null: the mode's own); capture: a click\n2026:/** a vehicle's ground after a step: a ray under it (tracks, the level, the terrain): on the ground or not, its slope (the\n2226:    if (!o.terrain && (!o.level || !o.level.rows)) throw new Error('my-3D2dge 3D: new E.World3D(game, { level: { rows: [...], legend: {...} } }) needs a level written as text (or { terr\n2238:    /** the level: its size (width, depth in units; mw, mh in tiles), bottom (where a fall is lost), marks; terrain: the\n2241:    const L = this.level = o.terrain ? new Terrain(this, o.terrain) : new Level(this, o.level);\n2242:    this.terrain = o.terrain ? L : null;\n2262:    this.camera = new Camera3D(this, Object.assign({ far: this.terrain ? this.terrain.far * 1.1 : 9600 }, o.camera));\n2312:  flow() { return this.terrain ? new TerrainFlow() : new Flow(this.level); }\n2316:    if (this.terrain) { for (let k = 0; k < 60; k++) { const x = rnd() * L.width, y = rnd() * L.depth; if (!minDist || Math.hypot(x - fx, y - fy) >= minDist) return [x, y]; } return [L.\n2330:    return !hit && !(this.terrain && this.terrain.rayDist(x0, y0, z0, dx / L, dy / L, dz / L, L) !== null);\n2334:   *  ground (true: the level or the terrain) } or null. o: { skip: an actor (or several) it passes through (the shooter),\n2343:    if (this.terrain) {   // the ground beyond the colliders made so far (and under them: the same triangles)\n2344:      const tt = this.terrain.rayDist(x, y, z, dx, dy, dz, t === null ? len : t);\n2345:      if (tt !== null && (t === null || tt < t - .01)) { t = tt; owner = this.terrain; n = this.terrain.normal(x + dx * tt, y + dy * tt, [0, 0, 1]); }\n2349:    return { x: x + dx * t, y: y + dy * t, z: z + dz * t, nx: n[0], ny: n[1], nz: n[2], dist: t, actor: isActor ? owner : null, prop: owner && !isActor && owner !== this.terrain ? owner\n2405:  /** the ground's surface tag at (x, y): a track's, else the level's ground under it (a terrain: null) */\n2408:    if (this.terrain) return null;\n2583:    if (this.level.stream) this.level.stream(this);   // (a terrain: the heightfields near the actors)\n2967:  /** what a frame needs before it draws: the terrain's meshes for where the camera is (all of them the first time), the\n2971:    if (this.terrain) this.terrain.drawStream(this, cp.x * U, cp.z * U, cp.y * U, this._warm ? TERRAIN_BUILDS : Infinity);","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ea1b61d-e1b8-4350-be76-ae4a4cbc51a9","uuid":"f90ce0c0-10a8-4be7-9824-6091d77545d7","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:28:59.877Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":" * 1. SETUP  units, helpers, collision groups, the page's renderer (World3D.init)\n * 2. TEXTURES AND MATERIALS  everything drawn by code, pixel by pixel, baked into crisp (nearest) textures\n * 3. LEVEL  written as text, one character per floor t