through, then\n12: * then the ship), a terrain (the sea, islands, the coast, the base's plateau, mountains round the bay), Dialog's radio.\n22:  /* ---- THE WORLD: a terrain. The sea (height 0), rock islands by the rail, the coast (a diagonal line: x + y = 30,500),\n30:    const db = Math.hypot(x - BAY[0], y - BAY[1]); if (db < 3000) h *= sstep(2200, 3000, db);   // the bay: sea inside the mountains\n37:    if (z < 1.5) { const w = vn(x / 260, y / 260); out[0] = 30 + w * 20 + n * 8; out[1] = 90 + w * 40 + n * 10; out[2] = 170 + w * 40; return out; }   // the sea\n70:  BOOT.push(['The sea and the base', () => {\n--- flight terrain\nsrc/starter3d/60-flight.js:71:    world = new W3(game, { terrain: { size: 32768, cell: 64, chunk: 32, height, color, far: 9000, physics: 0, detail: 1.1, rock: { colors: ['#8a8478', '#a09a8c', '#6e685e', '#b4ad9c'], band: 40, slope: [.4, .6]\nsrc/starter3d/30-shooter.js:9: * THE 3D: the ground is a terrain (world terrain: a height and a color function, streamed in chunks for the physics\nsrc/starter3d/30-shooter.js:2063:    world = new W3(game, { terrain: { size: SIZE, cell: 32, chunk: 32, height, color, far: 17000, physics: 1400, detail: 1.2, rock: { colors: ['#a8644a', '#c47e5a', '#8e523c', '#d0946a', '#b06e50', '#7a4632'\nsrc/starter3d/50-racing.js:13: * the shortcut, a dirt track without walls), world.vehicle (karts, their drivers seated), E.Race (the drive module:\nsrc/starter3d/50-racing.js:82:      const c = CAST[ci], g = grid[k], v = world.vehicle({ kind: 'kart', x: g.x, y: g.y, angle: g.angle, color: c.kart, rig: rigOf(c) });\n--- shake\n33:- new E.Game({ ..., bg: null }): its canvas is clear, and the HUD draws on it over the 3D picture (r.overlay, r.text,\n88:    r.overlay(g => { E.ui.hearts(g, 6, 6, Math.max(0, hp), 3); E.font.text(g, 'GEMS ' + gems.length, 6, 18, '#bff8ff'); });\n118:world instead of the level: below), overlay: { fov } (first person: below), onDraw: (world, r) => {} (your own 3D drawing\n242:in by world.ray). overlay: { fov } makes world.overlay = { scene, camera, pen, on }: drawn after the world, its depth\n243:cleared (the gun never sinks into a wall), lit like the world. overlay.pen is a pen in the eye's frame (engine units: x\n1115: * drew, for one frame, what it last held: zeros (on the overlay, whose camera is the origin, a screen of outline ink) or\n1170:/** the pen's batches in a scene: the world's own (shadows, tagged for the filters' mask), or the overlay's (sc: its scene;\n1171: *  no shadows, untagged: the overlay draws straight to the screen after the filter) */\n2266:    /** overlay: a scene of your own drawn over the world after it (its depth cleared first), from its own camera at the\n2270:    if (o.overlay) this._makeOverlay(o.overlay);\n2272:     *  (world.pen, overlay.pen, glows; a last touch to camera.pose) for every frame, whichever scene draws the world */\n2832:  /* the overlay (a view model): its own scene and camera, lit by the world's sky and sun as the camera sees them */\n2839:    this.overlay = { scene: sc, camera: cam, pen, on: o.on !== false, light: o.light ?? 1, _amb: amb, _sun: sun };\n2842:    const ov = this.overlay, A = this._ambient, q = _q0.copy(c3.quaternion).invert().premultiply(ov.camera.quaternion);\n2900:    const R = PAGE.renderer; if (!R) { this._queue.arcs.length = this._queue.glows.length = 0; for (const b of Object.values(this.B)) b.begin(); if (this.overlay) for (const b of Object.values(th\n2939:    // (the pens' batches hold what the game drew with world.pen and overlay.pen before this; they empty after the render)\n2940:    const OB = this.overlay && this.overlay.pen.B;\n2968:   *  sky's dome round the camera, the overlay's light and shape */\n2973:    if (this.overlay) { const oc = this.overlay.camera; oc.aspect = rw[0] / rw[1]; oc.updateProjectionMatrix(); this._lightOverlay(c3); }\n3113:      r.overlay(g => E.font.text(g, p.text, Math.round(s[0]), Math.round(s[1]), p.color, { align: 'center', scale: p.scale || 1, outli