{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Kan72wAbEToGbTD86r6UFw","type":"tool_result","content":"- `game.menu(name, o)`: open the menu (the corner's menu button and the touch START do it): a pausable scene (or a game started without scenes) pauses on its pause screen; any other scene, a title, waits under the settings. menu('settings') or menu('controls') opens that screen. Without a menu (menu: false, or the agent edition) it pauses a scene in play. o: { pause: false } opens it over a world that keeps stepping, as game.live does for every pause. Returns true when a menu opened\nAPI.md:137:- Prompts: `game.input.label('jump')` is that action's key or button on the player's device, after rebinding ('Space', 'A', '✕'). PlayStation symbols by default: `settings: [{ key: 'glyphs', value: 'playstation' }]` (a standard key without a label sets its default). A canvas title's OPTIONS: `game.menu('sett\n277:- `input.anyPressed()`: any action pressed this step (title screens: \"press any button\")\n492:- `game.hook(kind, fn)` †: a function of the game's own on the engine's clock: kind 'input' fn(dt) every step, paused or not, after the input is read (a host's guard, an idle timer); 'step' fn(dt) every update step in play, before the s\n655:- `slash.start(canCancel = false)`: begin a swing if idle (or when canCancel and already recovering). Returns true if it started\n656:- `slash.state`: what Humanoid.update wants as `attack` (null when idle)\n660:- `slash.phase = null`: 'wind' | 'active' | 'recover', or null when idle\n670:- `combo.state`: what Humanoid.update wants as `attack` (null when idle)\n672:- `combo.idle = 99`: seconds since the last hit ended\n710:- `rig.t`: seconds of its own clock (idle breathing, blinks)\n1236:- `new E.Arcade(game, o = {}) → arcade`: new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [] (the scores that give a life) or every (a life each that many points), credits: null (free play) or the coins a game takes, idle: 20, demo: 30, score\n1238:- `arcade.attract(dt)`: the attract mode, each step on the title: 'title', 'demo' (o.idle seconds without input; it lasts o.demo seconds or until endDemo()), 'scores' (o.scores seconds), then 'title' again; any input goes back to 'titl\n87:- 1116 Ui; E.Dialog: talk, E.Menu: menu\n317:- `input.touchArea()` †: where the touch buttons cover the screen, in screen pixels { x0, y0, x1, y1 } (the same space as r.W and r.H), or null while none show: keep a prompt or a box clear of it (a bottom E.Dialog does by itself)\n1064:- `game.audio.bus(name = 'sfx')`: a bus for a sound of the game's own (Web Audio nodes it makes on audio.ctx: a babble voice, a loop, an instrument) to connect to, so it follows the volume, the mute and the player's settings: 'sfx', 'music', 'voice' (its \n1066:- `game.audio.define(name, voice)`: add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 })\n1075:- `game.audio.sfx(what, o = {})`: Play a sound effect: a preset name ('jump', 'coin', 'hit', 'explode', ...), a voice object, or a list of voices. opts: { vol: 0..1, pitch: multiplier, vary: random pitch spread (default 0.03), step: a step of the music pl\n1084:- `game.audio.musicVolume = .5`, `game.audio.sfxVolume = 1`, `game.audio.voiceVolume = 1`: 0..1 for effects, music and the voice bus (bus('voice'))\n1087:- `game.audio.presets`: the named sound effects, sfx(name) plays one and define(name, voice) adds one\n1118:- `new E.Dialog(game, o = {}) → talk`: new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, place, color, nameColor, voice, width, bg, border, vars }): a dialog box that types its text; say() opens it, update(dt) and draw(r) run it\n1123:- `talk.say(text, o = {})`: open with one string or a list of strings (each starts a new page). opts: { name, onDone, choices, onChoice, portrait: rig (a live close-up of that Humanoid beside the text) or a function (g, x, y, size), portraitSize: 40, port\n1146:- `talk.voice = 'text'`: the sound effect each letter blips ('text'; null for silence), or a function (letter, index, dialog) called once for each letter as it types (a babble voice: Animalese; dialog.name is the speaker)\n1557:- `new E.Rhythm(game, o = {}) → rhythm` †: new E.Rhythm(game, { song, chart, lanes, windows, life, lead, voice, on }): see the manual\n1584:- `rhythm.voice` †: the calls' sound\n1064:- `game.audio.bus(name = 'sfx')`: a bus for a sound of the game's own (Web Audio nodes it makes on audio.ctx: a babble voice, a loop, an instrument) to connect to, so it follows the volume, the mute and the player's settings: 'sfx', 'music', 'voice' (its \n1084:- `game.audio.musicVolume = .5`, `game.audio.sfxVolume = 1`, `game.audio.voiceVolume = 1`: 0..1 for effects, music and the voice bus (bus('voice'))\n# Importing ready-made animation\n\nmy-3D2dge animates with code, but its rigs can also play animation made for 3D games. Imported animation is stored in one format that both people and AI models can read and edit: **readable key poses**, plain JSON with whole numbers (below)\n\n- **QUATERNIUS** (`src/mocap/sets/quaternius.js`): every free clip of [Quaternius' Universal Animation Library 1](https://quaternius.com/packs/universalanimationlibrary.html) and [Library 2](https://quaternius.com/packs/universalanimationli\n- **MESH2MOTION** (`src/mocap/sets/mesh2motion.js`): the human animations of [Mesh2Motion](https://github.com/Mesh2Motion/mesh2motion-app) (CC0), from three origins:\n  - 86 of Quaternius' clips as Mesh2Motion re-exported them (one defective copy is skipped);\n  - 75 clips its contributors animated (ladder, wall and pipe climbs, ledge hang, bow, backflip, dodges, crawling, flying, dances, emotes, deaths);\n  - 16 it motion-captured itself with a Sony mocopi suit (fishing, golf, cheers, salutes, turns).\n\n  That makes 177 clips, and every one records which origin it came from (see [Where each clip came from](#where-each-clip-came-from)).\n- **CMU** (`src/mocap/sets/cmu.js`): 60 moments cut from the [CMU Graphics Lab Motion Capture Database](http://mocap.cs.cmu.edu/) (2,548 takes, free for all uses), picked for what a game like Emberdeep needs: gaits (run, sneak, limp, clutch\n- **HERO** (`src/mocap/sets/hero.js`): the 15 clips Emberdeep's hero, the Wanderer, has adopted (see [The hero's clips](#the-heros-clips-in-emberdeep)): 8 from QUATERNIUS and 7 from MESH2MOTION, picked with `tools/anim-set.mjs`. It is the o\n\n`examples/mocap-lab.html` plays any of the sets (**G** switches) on two figures:\n\n- **a look-alike of the libraries' mannequin**: an orange figure with an egg-shaped head and purple joint rings. Its proportions and limb thickness are measured from the first library's own mesh.\n- **the engine's hero** (the Emberdeep swordsman, an HD `Humanoid`), playing the same clip retargeted to his chibi build. His cape and hair follow, and in sword clips his blade follows his fist.\n\nBoth work in every view, at any camera turn or zoom, in slow motion and frame by frame.\n\nTo bring in another library, follow [Adding a library, step by step](#adding-a-library-step-by-step); [Where to get more animation](#where-to-get-more-animation) lists the sources, what they cost and what each one takes.\n\n## Pipeline\n\n```\n.blend / .fbx / .bvh ──tools/to-glb.py──▶ .glb\nCMU takes (.asf + .amc) ──tools/cmu.mjs get──▶ .cache/cmu ──tools/anim-import.mjs --cmu──▶ src/mocap/sets/cmu.js\nlibraries (.glb) ──tools/anim-import.mjs──▶ src/mocap/sets/quaternius.js ──tools/anim-set.mjs──▶ src/mocap/sets/hero.js\n                                                     │                                                    │\n                                                     └──────────── Mocap.load(set) ◀──────────────────────┘\n                                                                        │\n                                              lib.sample(clip, t) ──▶ Mannequin.draw / Mocap.drive(humanoid)\n```\n\n1. **Import** (Node, no dependencies):\n\n   ```\n   node tools/anim-import.mjs UAL1.glb UAL2.glb --sources UAL1,UAL2 --name QUATERNIUS \\\n     --catalog src/mocap/catalogs/quaternius.json --out src/mocap/sets/quaternius.js\n47:const game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, bg: null, input: E.World3D.INPUT, menu: { settings: E.World3D.SETTINGS } });\n250:  E.World3D.SETTINGS in the game's menu lets the player pick the look, the picture, shadows and the filter.\n2912:    // the player's settings (World3D.SETTINGS), taken up when they change\n3287:/** the player's 3D settings for the pause menu (new E.Game({ menu: { settings: E.World3D.SETTINGS } })): Characters\n3289:World3D.SETTINGS = [\n3297:World3D.CONTROLS = { key: 'tank3d', label: 'Tank controls', group: 'Game', value: false, help: 'Up walks forward the way your character faces, down backs away, left and right turn it, whatever the camera does. Off: the stick moves it the way the camera looks.' };","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ea1b61d-e1b8-4350-be76-ae4a4cbc51a9","uuid":"4d8cb8bb-57b1-44f4-85a8-e04f22e8091c","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:44:22.133Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"- `game.menu(name, o)`: open the menu (the corner's menu button and the touch START do it): a pausable scene (or a game started without scenes) pauses on its pause screen; any other scene, a title, waits under the settings. menu('settings') or menu('controls') opens that screen. Without a menu (menu: false, or the agent edition) it pauses a scene in play. o: { pause: false } opens it over a world that keeps stepping, as game.live does for every pause. Returns true when a menu opened\nAPI.md:137:- Prompts: `game.input.label('jump')` is that action's key or button on the player's device, after rebinding ('Space', 'A', '✕'). PlayStation symbols by default: `settings: [{ key: 'glyphs', value: 'playstation' }]` (a standard key without a label sets its default). A canvas title's OPTIONS: `game.menu('sett\n277:- `input.anyPressed()`: any action pressed this step (title screens: \"press any button\")\n492:- `game.hook(kind, fn)` †: a function of the game's own on the engine's clock: kind 'input' fn(dt) every step, paused or not, after the input is read (a host's guard, an idle timer); 'step' fn(dt) every update step in play, before the s\n655:- `slash.start(canCancel = false)`: begin a swing if idle (or when canCancel and already recovering). Returns true if it started\n656:- `slash.state`: what Humanoid.update wants as `attack` (null when idle)\n660:- `slash.phase = null`: 'wind' | 'active' | 'recover', or null when idle\n670:- `combo.state`: what Humanoid.update wants as `attack` (null when idle)\n672:- `combo.idle = 99`: seconds since the last hit ended\n710:- `rig.t`: seconds of its own clock (idle breathing, blinks)\n1236:- `new E.Arcade(game, o = {}) → arcade`: new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [] (the scores that give a life) or every (a life each that many points), credits: null (free play) or the coins a game takes, idle: 20, demo: 30, score\n1238:- `arcade.attract(dt)`: the attract mode, each step on the title: 'title', 'demo' (o.idle seconds without input; it lasts o.demo seconds or until endDemo()), 'scores' (o.scores seconds), then 'title' again; any input goes back to 'titl\n87:- 1116 Ui; E.Dialog: talk, E.Menu: menu\n317:- `input.touchArea()` †: where the touch buttons cover the screen, in screen pixels { x0, y0, x1, y1 } (the same space as r.W and r.H), or null while none show: keep a prompt or a box clear of it (a bottom E.Dialog does by itself)\n1064:- `game.audio.bus(name = 'sfx')`: a bus for a sound of the game's own (Web Audio nodes it makes on audio.ctx: a babble voice, a loop, an instrument) to connect to, so it follows the volume, the mute and the player's settings: 'sfx', 'music', 'voice' (its \n1066:- `game.audio.define(name, voice)`: add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 })\n1075:- `game.audio.sfx(what, o = {})`: Play a sound effect: a preset name ('jump', 'coin', 'hit', 'explode', ...), a voice object, or a list of voices. opts: { vol: 0..1, pitch: multiplier, vary: random pitch spread (default 0.03), step: a step of the music pl\n1084:- `game.audio.musicVolume = .5`, `game.audio.sfxVolume = 1`, `game.audio.voiceVolume = 1`: 0..1 for effects, music and the voice bus (bus('voice'))\n1087:- `game.audio.presets`: the named sound effects, sfx(name) plays one and define(name, voice) adds one\n1118:- `new E.Dialog(game, o = {}) → talk`: new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, place, color, nameColor, voice, width, bg, border, vars }): a dialog box that types its text; say() opens it, update(dt) and draw(r) run it\n1123:- `talk.say(text, o = {})`: open with one string or a list of strings (each starts a new page). opts: { name, onDone, choices, onChoice, portrait: rig (a live close-up of that Humanoid beside the text) or a function (g, x, y, size), portraitSize: 40, port\n1146:- `talk.voice = 'text'`: the sound effect each letter blips ('text'; null for silence), or a function (letter, index, dialog) called once for each letter as it types (a babble voice: Animalese; dialog.name is the speaker)\n1557:- `new E.Rhythm(game, o = {}) → rhythm` †: new E.Rhythm(game, { song, chart, lanes, windows, life, lead, voice, on }): see the manual\n1584:- `rhythm.voice` †: the calls' sound\n1064:- `game.audio.bus(name = 'sfx')`: a bus for a sound of the game's own (Web Audio nodes it makes on audio.ctx: a babble voice, a loop, an instrument) to connect to, so it follows the volume, the mute and the player's settings: 'sfx', 'music', 'voice' (its \n1084:- `game.audio.musicVolume = .5`, `game.audio.sfxVolume = 1`, `game.audio.voiceVolume = 1`: 0..1 for effects, music and the voice bus (bus('voice'))\n# Importing ready-made animation\n\nmy-3D2dge animates with code, but its rigs can also play animation made for 3D games. Imported animation is stored in one format that both people and AI models can read and edit: **readable key poses**, plain JSON with whole numbers (below)\n\n- **QUATERNIUS** (`src/mocap/sets/quaternius.js`): every free clip of [Quaternius' Universal Animation Library 1](https://quaternius.com/packs/universalanimationlibrary.html) and [Library 2](https://quaternius.com/packs/universalanimationli\n- **MESH2MOTION** (`src/mocap/sets/mesh2motion.js`): the human animations of [Mesh2Motion](https://github.com/Mesh2Motion/mesh2motion-app) (CC0), from three origins:\n  - 86 of Quaternius' clips as Mesh2Motion re-exported them (one defective copy is skipped);\n  - 75 clips its contributors animated (ladder, wall and pipe climbs, ledge hang, bow, backflip, dodges, crawling, flying, dances, emotes, deaths);\n  - 16 it motion-captured itself with a Sony mocopi suit (fishing, golf, cheers, salutes, turns).\n\n  That makes 177 clips, and every one records which origin it came from (see [Where each clip came from](#where-each-clip-came-from)).\n- **CMU** (`src/mocap/sets/cmu.js`): 60 moments cut from the [CMU Graphics Lab Motion Capture Database](http://mocap.cs.cmu.edu/) (2,548 takes, free for all uses), picked for what a game like Emberdeep needs: gaits (run, sneak, limp, clutch\n- **HERO** (`src/mocap/sets/hero.js`): the 15 clips Emberdeep's hero, the Wanderer, has adopted (see [The hero's clips](#the-heros-clips-in-emberdeep)): 8 from QUATERNIUS and 7 from MESH2MOTION, picked with `tools/anim-set.mjs`. It is the o\n\n`examples/mocap-lab.html` plays any of the sets (**G** switches) on two figures:\n\n- **a look-alike of the libraries' mannequin**: an orange figure with an egg-shaped head and purple joint rings. Its proportions and limb thickness are measured from the first library's own mesh.\n- **the engine's hero** (the Emberdeep swordsman, an HD `Humanoid`), playing the same clip retargeted to his chibi build. His cape and hair follow, and in sword clips his blade follows his fist.\n\nBoth work in every view, at any camera turn or zoom, in slow motion and frame by frame.\n\nTo bring in another library, follow [Adding a library, step by step](#adding-a-library-step-by-step); [Where to get more animation](#where-to-get-more-animation) lists the sources, what they cost and what each one takes.\n\n## Pipeline\n\n```\n.blend / .fbx / .bvh ──tools/to-glb.py──▶ .glb\nCMU takes (.asf + .amc) ──tools/cmu.mjs get──▶ .cache/cmu ──tools/anim-import.mjs --cmu──▶ src/mocap/sets/cmu.js\nlibraries (.glb) ──tools/anim-import.mjs──▶ src/mocap/sets/quaternius.js ──tools/anim-set.mjs──▶ src/mocap/sets/hero.js\n                                                     │                                                    │\n                                                     └──────────── Mocap.load(set) ◀──────────────────────┘\n                                                                        │\n                                              lib.sample(clip, t) ──▶ Mannequin.draw / Mocap.drive(humanoid)\n```\n\n1. **Import** (Node, no dependencies):\n\n   ```\n   node tools/anim-import.mjs UAL1.glb UAL2.glb --sources UAL1,UAL2 --name QUATERNIUS \\\n     --catalog src/mocap/catalogs/quaternius.json --out src/mocap/sets/quaternius.js\n47:const game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, bg: null, input: E.World3D.INPUT, menu: { settings: E.World3D.SETTINGS } });\n250:  E.World3D.SETTINGS in the game's menu lets the player pick the look, the picture, shadows and the filter.\n2912:    // the player's settings (World3D.SETTINGS), taken up when they change\n3287:/** the player's 3D settings for the pause menu (new E.Game({ menu: { settings: E.World3D.SETTINGS } })): Characters\n3289:World3D.SETTINGS = [\n3297:World3D.CONTROLS = { key: 'tank3d', label: 'Tank controls', group: 'Game', value: false, help: 'Up walks forward the way your character faces, down backs away, left and right turn it, whatever the camera does. Off: the stick moves it the way the camera looks.' };","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Kan72wAbEToGbTD86r6UFw","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
