{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RXhcQCFQsY7gqvUxJgp9bY","type":"tool_result","content":"4://      WebGPURenderer and node materials only (no WebGLRenderer, ShaderMaterial, onBeforeCompile, EffectComposer,\n5://      addons), no WebGPU-only compute or storage buffers, nothing read back from the GPU; the import map points at\n9://   3. every 3D kit, served as Vercel serves it (/kits/3d-<slice>, /3d), on WebGL 2 and on WebGPU (headless Chromium runs\n10://      WebGPU on SwiftShader, through a stand-in canvas): no page errors, the title\n11://      draws, each slice starts; each slice's proof run gives the same hash twice and on both backends (the game never\n14://   3b. shapes (world.shape: the 2D engine's entries in 3D): every core shape builds and draws on WebGL 2 and on WebGPU (its\n16://      sheet of every core shape in 3D beside its 2D picture (check-output/kit3d/shapes-<backend>.png: read it)\n24://   3d. vehicles, tracks, flight and split screen, on a page of their own, on WebGL 2 and on WebGPU: a kart takes to its\n29://      bounds, seek picks the one in its cone and in sight; all of it twice the same and the same on both backends; a\n30://      split screen draws two views through world.cameras (check-output/kit3d/split-<backend>.png: read it), side by side\n31://      and stacked (viewport 0 on top, as the 2D layout has it: split-rows-<backend>.png)\n32://   3e. first person with the cel filter, on both backends: the filtered hall and the overlay's gun are both drawn\n33://      (check-output/kit3d/fps-cel-<backend>.png)\n51:  [/\\bWebGLRenderer\\b/, 'WebGLRenderer (use WebGPURenderer: it falls back to WebGL 2 by itself)'],\n53:  [/\\bonBeforeCompile\\b/, 'onBeforeCompile (not run by WebGPURenderer)'],\n55:  [/\\bcompute\\s*\\(|\\bStorageBufferAttribute\\b|\\bstorage\\s*\\(|\\bcomputeAsync\\b/, 'compute shaders or storage buffers (WebGPU only)'],\n247:const browser = await chromium.launch({ executablePath: process