{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K8HWVj9STJfB3J6QA12CyW","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Far Cry 2 characters list factions UFLL APR The Jackal mercenaries buddies locations Leboa-Sako Bowa-Seko\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Far Cry 2\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Far_Cry_2\"},{\"title\":\"Far Cry 2 Characters\",\"url\":\"https://shapes.inc/fandom/far-cry-2/characters\"},{\"title\":\"far cry 2 announced\",\"url\":\"https://itwire.com/your-it-news/entertainment/far-cry-2-announced\"},{\"title\":\"Far Cry 2 - interview\",\"url\":\"https://gamesradar.com/far-cry-2-interview/3\"},{\"title\":\"far cry 2\",\"url\":\"https://www.mobygames.com/game/j2me/far-cry-2_\"},{\"title\":\"Far Cry 2 - updated hands-on\",\"url\":\"https://gamesradar.com/far-cry-2-updated-hands-on\"},{\"title\":\"Far Cry 2\",\"url\":\"https://bafybeiemxf5abjwjbikoz4mc3a3dla6ual3jsgpdr4cjr3oz3evfyavhwq.ipfs.4everland.io/wiki/Far_Cry_2.html\"},{\"title\":\"bellaonline.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.bellaonline.com/articles/art24696.asp\"},{\"title\":\"Sunday 28 October 2012\",\"url\":\"https://thewertzone.blogspot.com/2012/10/far-cry-2_28.html\"},{\"title\":\"techenclave.com\",\"url\":\"https://techenclave.com/t/far-cry-2-official-trailer/117998\"},{\"title\":\"Far Cry 2 Review\",\"url\":\"https://www.gamesxtreme.com/article/3565/far-cry-2-review\"},{\"title\":\"Far Cry 2\",\"url\":\"https://ipfs.ssi.eecc.de/ipns/en.wikipedia-on-ipfs.org/wiki/Far_Cry_2\"},{\"title\":\"far cry 2\",\"url\":\"https://videogamegeek.com/videogame/74422/far-cry-2\"},{\"title\":\"Far Cry Wiki\",\"url\":\"https://farcry.fandom.com/wiki/Far_Cry_factions\"},{\"title\":\"far cry 2 far cry 2 is open world first\",\"url\":\"https://gamingking.blogspot.com/2013/10/far-cry-2-far-cry-2-is-open-world-first.html\"},{\"title\":\"Giant Bomb Review\",\"url\":\"https://www.giantbomb.com/reviews/far-cry-2-review/1900-76/\"},{\"title\":\"www.moddb.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.moddb.com/games/far-cry-2/addons/hans\"},{\"title\":\"Unraveling The Chaos: A Comprehensive Far Cry 2 Review\",\"url\":\"https://br2.imexhs.com/their-involvement/unraveling-the-chaos-a-comprehensive-far-cry-2-review.html\"},{\"title\":\"Far Cry 2\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.com/wiki/Far_Cry_2\"}]\n\nThe search confirmed the two factions and some characters, but it didn't return anything on Leboa-Sako or Bowa-Seko.\n\n- **Factions:** One listing names the UFLL (United Front for Liberation and Labor) and the APR (Alliance for Popular Resistance). The civil war is between the UFLL and the APR, who are indistinguishable apart from the missions that they give you.\n- **Characters:** Listings name Jack Carver, the Warlord, The Jackal, and Marty Alencar. A fuller roster includes Warren Clyde, Nasreen Davar, Hakim Echebbi, Paul Ferenc, Flora Guillen, Andre Hyppolite, Josip Idromeno, and Frank Bilders. The Jackal is described as an antagonist and arms dealer.\n- **Mercenaries and buddies:** The playable character is selected from a pool of nine available mercenaries; the remaining eight and some other non-playable mercenary characters are distributed through the world once the game starts. Those playable mercenaries found in the open world are called Buddies. If Buddies are injured on missions and not healed in time, they die and will be permanently removed from the rest of the game.\n- **Locations:** One listing names Shanty Town, a Dogon village, a desert water hole, savannah, and jungle, along with a desert crash site. The game is split between a northern territory and a southern one, over a combined total of 50km of Africa.\n\nThe sources are of mixed quality. The character and location lists come from pre-release or fan-compiled pages, so they may be incomplete or inaccurate. I found no source for Leboa-Sako or Bowa-Seko, so I'd check the Far Cry 2 wiki or a full map guide for those.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ea1b61d-e1b8-4350-be76-ae4a4cbc51a9","uuid":"83c690e9-3757-4295-95ef-54fc5773ee86","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:50:10.638Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Far Cry 2 characters list factions UFLL APR The Jackal mercenaries buddies locations Leboa-Sako Bowa-Seko","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01QnrnopHDPxm63oV4bRQUkE","content":[{"title":"Far Cry 2","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Far_Cry_2"},{"title":"Far Cry 2 Characters","url":"https://shapes.inc/fandom/far-cry-2/characters"},{"title":"far cry 2 announced","url":"https://itwire.com/your-it-news/entertainment/far-cry-2-announced"},{"title":"Far Cry 2 - interview","url":"https://gamesradar.com/far-cry-2-interview/3"},{"title":"far cry 2","url":"https://www.mobygames.com/game/j2me/far-cry-2_"},{"title":"Far Cry 2 - updated hands-on","url":"https://gamesradar.com/far-cry-2-updated-hands-on"},{"title":"Far Cry 2","url":"https://bafybeiemxf5abjwjbikoz4mc3a3dla6ual3jsgpdr4cjr3oz3evfyavhwq.ipfs.4everland.io/wiki/Far_Cry_2.html"},{"title":"bellaonline.com","url":"https://www.bellaonline.com/articles/art24696.asp"},{"title":"Sunday 28 October 2012","url":"https://thewertzone.blogspot.com/2012/10/far-cry-2_28.html"},{"title":"techenclave.com","url":"https://techenclave.com/t/far-cry-2-official-trailer/117998"},{"title":"Far Cry 2 Review","url":"https://www.gamesxtreme.com/article/3565/far-cry-2-review"},{"title":"Far Cry 2","url":"https://ipfs.ssi.eecc.de/ipns/en.wikipedia-on-ipfs.org/wiki/Far_Cry_2"},{"title":"far cry 2","url":"https://videogamegeek.com/videogame/74422/far-cry-2"},{"title":"Far Cry Wiki","url":"https://farcry.fandom.com/wiki/Far_Cry_factions"},{"title":"far cry 2 far cry 2 is open world first","url":"https://gamingking.blogspot.com/2013/10/far-cry-2-far-cry-2-is-open-world-first.html"},{"title":"Giant Bomb Review","url":"https://www.giantbomb.com/reviews/far-cry-2-review/1900-76/"},{"title":"www.moddb.com","url":"https://www.moddb.com/games/far-cry-2/addons/hans"},{"title":"Unraveling The Chaos: A Comprehensive Far Cry 2 Review","url":"https://br2.imexhs.com/their-involvement/unraveling-the-chaos-a-comprehensive-far-cry-2-review.html"},{"title":"Far Cry 2","url":"https://en.wikipedia.com/wiki/Far_Cry_2"}]},"The search confirmed the two factions and some characters, but it didn't return anything on Leboa-Sako or Bowa-Seko.\n\n- **Factions:** One listing names the UFLL (United Front for Liberation and Labor) and the APR (Alliance for Popular Resistance). The civil war is between the UFLL and the APR, who are indistinguishable apart from the missions that they give you.\n- **Characters:** Listings name Jack Carver, the Warlord, The Jackal, and Marty Alencar. A fuller roster includes Warren Clyde, Nasreen Davar, Hakim Echebbi, Paul Ferenc, Flora Guillen, Andre Hyppolite, Josip Idromeno, and Frank Bilders. The Jackal is described as an antagonist and arms dealer.\n- **Mercenaries and buddies:** The playable character is selected from a pool of nine available mercenaries; the remaining eight and some other non-playable mercenary characters are distributed through the world once the game starts. Those playable mercenaries found in the open world are called Buddies. If Buddies are injured on missions and not healed in time, they die and will be permanently removed from the rest of the game.\n- **Locations:** One listing names Shanty Town, a Dogon village, a desert water hole, savannah, and jungle, along with a desert crash site. The game is split between a northern territory and a southern one, over a combined total of 50km of Africa.\n\nThe sources are of mixed quality. The character and location lists come from pre-release or fan-compiled pages, so they may be incomplete or inaccurate. I found no source for Leboa-Sako or Bowa-Seko, so I'd check the Far Cry 2 wiki or a full map guide for those."],"durationSeconds":6.775188209000044,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01K8HWVj9STJfB3J6QA12CyW","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LrXGciZpHzKmJ6enwCXqnR","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Far Cry 2 game design features fire propagation weapon degradation jamming malaria buddy system diegetic map\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Far Cry 2\",\"url\":\"https://giantbomb.com/wiki/Games/Far_Cry_2\"},{\"title\":\"www.giantbomb.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.giantbomb.com/games/3030-20665/\"},{\"title\":\"www.giantbomb.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.giantbomb.com/wd/3030-20665/\"},{\"title\":\"www.mobygames.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.mobygames.com/game/37038/\"},{\"title\":\"Far Cry 2\",\"url\":\"https://ipfs.ssi.eecc.de/ipns/en.wikipedia-on-ipfs.org/wiki/Far_Cry_2\"},{\"title\":\"giantbomb.com\",\"url\":\"https://giantbomb.com/far-cry-2/3030-20665/\"},{\"title\":\"farcry 2.114772\",\"url\":\"https://forums.tomshardware.com/threads/farcry-2.114772\"},{\"title\":\"Far Cry 2\",\"url\":\"https://bafybeiemxf5abjwjbikoz4mc3a3dla6ual3jsgpdr4cjr3oz3evfyavhwq.ipfs.4everland.io/wiki/Far_Cry_2.html\"},{\"title\":\"[Review] Far Cry 2\",\"url\":\"https://bluedemonarchive.blogspot.com/2021/07/far-cry-2.html\"},{\"title\":\"Mechanics 7: Heart of Darkness (Far Cry 2)\",\"url\":\"https://gamedev.net/blogs/entry/1844402-mechanics-7-heart-of-darkness-far-cry-2\"},{\"title\":\"de.wikipedia.org\",\"url\":\"https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benutzer:ColdCut/FarCry2\"},{\"title\":\"far cry 2 far cry 2 is open world first\",\"url\":\"https://gamingking.blogspot.com/2013/10/far-cry-2-far-cry-2-is-open-world-first.html\"},{\"title\":\"far cry 2 425437961669181477\",\"url\":\"https://discord.com/game/far-cry-2-425437961669181477\"},{\"title\":\"store.steampowered.com\",\"url\":\"https://store.steampowered.com/app/19900/  Instructions\"},{\"title\":\"far cry 2\",\"url\":\"https://mobygames.com/game/37038/far-cry-2\"},{\"title\":\"store.steampowered.com\",\"url\":\"https://store.steampowered.com/app/19900?l=polish\"},{\"title\":\"Far Cry 2\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.com/wiki/Far_Cry_2\"}]\n\nFar Cry 2 (Ubisoft Montreal, 2008) matches most of the features you listed, though the search results contain little detail on the buddy system and nothing on the diegetic map beyond a basic description.\n\n- **Fire propagation:** Sources describe a fire mechanic in which a small blaze can grow into large brush fires, and the player can use it either for or against themselves. A unique fire propagation mechanism, which allows a small fire to spread and eventually cause large brush fires, may be used either to the player's advantage during combat or against the player.\n- **Weapon degradation and jamming:** Worn weapons can jam and need several seconds to clear, and heavily decayed ones can break outright. Weapons in poor shape have a chance of jamming, requiring several seconds to clear, and weapons in a severe state of decay can break during usage, rendering the weapon unusable. Another review notes that guns get dirty and become more prone to jamming with use, and that buying new weapons from shops avoids the issue. Weapon degradation is only an issue if you are picking up trash guns out of the ground instead of buying your own.\n- **Malaria:** The player contracts malaria early on. As earlier upon your arrival, you contract malaria.\n- **Buddy system:** Buddies are NPC allies, and buddy missions raise the player's reputation in the game world and improve how the buddy sees the player. There are also, special buddy-missions. In these scenarios, you go and do a job for a buddy. Which increases your reputation, in the game world. And it increases your buddies view of you.\n- **Map:** The player must hold a physical map and use a handheld navigation device, and the device updates automatically as the player travels. The player needs to hold a physical map and use a handheld navigation system (which highly resembles a military-type GPS) to get around, but they are automatically updated as the player travels through the environment. The fan-wiki source also says players can tag objects and locations on the map. The player is able to tag certain objects and locations such as cars, sniper towers, ammo pickups and buildings, so that they are able to monitor them on their map.\n\nI found no source explicitly calling the map \"diegetic\" in the design-theory sense, so that term is my inference from the physical-map description. The search results are mostly fan sites, blogs, and forums, so the more specific claims would benefit from a check against Ubisoft's materials or a developer postmortem.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ea1b61d-e1b8-4350-be76-ae4a4cbc51a9","uuid":"9df9d0c3-6afe-45bc-8111-507d2ad8e13b","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:50:11.210Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Far Cry 2 game design features fire propagation weapon degradation jamming malaria buddy system diegetic map","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01BXrfrfKhBB8NZxpkKVxim4","content":[{"title":"Far Cry 2","url":"https://giantbomb.com/wiki/Games/Far_Cry_2"},{"title":"www.giantbomb.com","url":"https://www.giantbomb.com/games/3030-20665/"},{"title":"www.giantbomb.com","url":"https://www.giantbomb.com/wd/3030-20665/"},{"title":"www.mobygames.com","url":"https://www.mobygames.com/game/37038/"},{"title":"Far Cry 2","url":"https://ipfs.ssi.eecc.de/ipns/en.wikipedia-on-ipfs.org/wiki/Far_Cry_2"},{"title":"giantbomb.com","url":"https://giantbomb.com/far-cry-2/3030-20665/"},{"title":"farcry 2.114772","url":"https://forums.tomshardware.com/threads/farcry-2.114772"},{"title":"Far Cry 2","url":"https://bafybeiemxf5abjwjbikoz4mc3a3dla6ual3jsgpdr4cjr3oz3evfyavhwq.ipfs.4everland.io/wiki/Far_Cry_2.html"},{"title":"[Review] Far Cry 2","url":"https://bluedemonarchive.blogspot.com/2021/07/far-cry-2.html"},{"title":"Mechanics 7: Heart of Darkness (Far Cry 2)","url":"https://gamedev.net/blogs/entry/1844402-mechanics-7-heart-of-darkness-far-cry-2"},{"title":"de.wikipedia.org","url":"https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benutzer:ColdCut/FarCry2"},{"title":"far cry 2 far cry 2 is open world first","url":"https://gamingking.blogspot.com/2013/10/far-cry-2-far-cry-2-is-open-world-first.html"},{"title":"far cry 2 425437961669181477","url":"https://discord.com/game/far-cry-2-425437961669181477"},{"title":"store.steampowered.com","url":"https://store.steampowered.com/app/19900/  Instructions"},{"title":"far cry 2","url":"https://mobygames.com/game/37038/far-cry-2"},{"title":"store.steampowered.com","url":"https://store.steampowered.com/app/19900?l=polish"},{"title":"Far Cry 2","url":"https://en.wikipedia.com/wiki/Far_Cry_2"}]},"Far Cry 2 (Ubisoft Montreal, 2008) matches most of the features you listed, though the search results contain little detail on the buddy system and nothing on the diegetic map beyond a basic description.\n\n- **Fire propagation:** Sources describe a fire mechanic in which a small blaze can grow into large brush fires, and the player can use it either for or against themselves. A unique fire propagation mechanism, which allows a small fire to spread and eventually cause large brush fires, may be used either to the player's advantage during combat or against the player.\n- **Weapon degradation and jamming:** Worn weapons can jam and need several seconds to clear, and heavily decayed ones can break outright. Weapons in poor shape have a chance of jamming, requiring several seconds to clear, and weapons in a severe state of decay can break during usage, rendering the weapon unusable. Another review notes that guns get dirty and become more prone to jamming with use, and that buying new weapons from shops avoids the issue. Weapon degradation is only an issue if you are picking up trash guns out of the ground instead of buying your own.\n- **Malaria:** The player contracts malaria early on. As earlier upon your arrival, you contract malaria.\n- **Buddy system:** Buddies are NPC allies, and buddy missions raise the player's reputation in the game world and improve how the buddy sees the player. There are also, special buddy-missions. In these scenarios, you go and do a job for a buddy. Which increases your reputation, in the game world. And it increases your buddies view of you.\n- **Map:** The player must hold a physical map and use a handheld navigation device, and the device updates automatically as the player travels. The player needs to hold a physical map and use a handheld navigation system (which highly resembles a military-type GPS) to get around, but they are automatically updated as the player travels through the environment. The fan-wiki source also says players can tag objects and locations on the map. The player is able to tag certain objects and locations such as cars, sniper towers, ammo pickups and buildings, so that they are able to monitor them on their map.\n\nI found no source explicitly calling the map \"diegetic\" in the design-theory sense, so that term is my inference from the physical-map description. The search results are mostly fan sites, blogs, and forums, so the more specific claims would benefit from a check against Ubisoft's materials or a developer postmortem."],"durationSeconds":7.836185792000033,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01LrXGciZpHzKmJ6enwCXqnR","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
