{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0167SwJVB2BaSkDkg3fWV2UW","type":"tool_result","content":"  /** draw everything once, empty (scaled to nothing), so every material builds its shaders and GPU pipelines now, shadow\n   *  passes too, and none stalls a frame mid-game */\n  _warmUp(cam, view) {\n    this._warm = true;\n    this._arcs.prepare(8); this._rings.prepare(12); this._ribbons.prepare(6); this.atlas.prepare(view, 1);\n    const Z = new THREE.Matrix4().makeScale(0, 0, 0), M = this._propMesh, inst = [M.crate, M.barrel];\n    for (const b of [...Object.values(this.B), ...Object.values(this.part), ...(this.overlay ? Object.values(this.overlay.pen.B) : [])]) { inst.push(b.mesh); if (b.shell) inst.push(b.shell); }\n    for (const pg of this.atlas.pages) inst.push(pg.mesh);\n    inst.push(this._shapeKit.probe, this._shapeKit.probeShell);   // (the shapes' shaders, before any is placed)\n    const counts = inst.map(m => m.count), pools = [...this._arcs.list, ...this._rings.list, ...this._ribbons.list], vis = pools.map(m => m.visible);\n    for (const m of inst) { m.setMatrixAt(0, Z); m.instanceMatrix.clearUpdateRanges(); m.instanceMatrix.needsUpdate = true; m.count = 1; }\n    for (const m of pools) m.visible = true;\n    const sh = this._shadowLights.map(L => [L.castShadow, L.intensity]), gl = this._glowLights.map(L => L.intensity), ul = this._userLights.map(L => L.intensity), sp = this._spots.map(L => [L.castShadow, L.intensity]);\n    for (const L of [...this._shadowLights, ...this._glowLights, ...this._userLights, ...this._spots]) { L.intensity = Math.max(L.intensity, .001); }\n    this._shadowLights.forEach(L => { L.castShadow = true; }); this._spots.forEach(L => { L.castShadow = this.shadows; });\n    const capes = this.capes.mesh, cd = capes.geometry.drawRange.count, cv = capes.visible; capes.geometry.setDrawRange(0, 6); capes.visible = true;\n    const ovHid = []; if (this.overlay) this.overlay.scene.traverse(x => { if (!x.visible) { ovHid.push(x); x.visible = true; } });\n    const ovOn = this.overlay && this.overlay.on; if (this.overlay) this.overlay.on = true;\n    const culled = []; this.scene.traverse(x => { if (x.isMesh && x.frustumCulled) { culled.push(x); x.frustumCulled = false; } });   // (every caster in every light's shadow too: a torch's culls what lies outside it, whose shadow pipeline was then built mid-game, the first time a torch came near)\n    this._render(cam);\n    for (const x of culled) x.frustumCulled = true;\n    for (const x of ovHid) x.visible = false; if (this.overlay) this.overlay.on = ovOn;\n    capes.geometry.setDrawRange(0, cd); capes.visible = cv;\n    this._shadowLights.forEach((L, i) => { L.castShadow = sh[i][0]; L.intensity = sh[i][1]; }); this._glowLights.forEach((L, i) => { L.intensity = gl[i]; }); this._userLights.forEach((L, i) => { L.intensity = ul[i]; }); this._spots.forEach((L, i) => { L.castShadow = sp[i][0]; L.intensity = sp[i][1];\n    inst.forEach((m, i) => { m.count = counts[i]; }); pools.forEach((m, i) => { m.visible = vis[i]; });\n  },\n  /** build every shader now (a boot step): one warm-up frame drawn off the record (three r182's compileAsync leaves a\n   *  light's shadow without its map, so the warm-up draws instead) */\n  prepare() {\n    if (!PAGE.renderer) return this;\n\n247:  world.look = 'card' | 'puppet'; world.res = 'pixels' | 'balanced' | 'full'; world.shadows; world.outlines\n2234:    this.look = o.look || st.look3d || 'card'; this.res = RES.includes(o.res) ? o.res : RES.includes(st.picture3d) ? st.picture3d : 'pixels';\n2913:    const st = g.settings || {}, sk = [st.look3d, st.picture3d, st.shadows3d, st.filter3d].join();\n2915:      if (this._sk !== undefined) { if (st.look3d) this.look = st.look3d; if (RES.includes(st.picture3d)) this.res = st.picture3d; if (st.shadows3d !== undefined) this.shadows = !!st.shadows3d; if (st.filter3d) this\n3291:  { key: 'picture3d', label: '3D picture', group: 'Display', value: 'pixels', options: [['pixels', 'Pixels'], ['balanced', 'Balanced'], ['full', 'Full']], help: 'Pixels: the game\\'s own resolution, chunky and fast. \n337:- `input.padAim = null` †: its right stick, or null when centered\n322:- `input.value(a)` †: how far action a is pressed, 0 to 1: a gamepad button by its travel (the triggers, even short of a press), a stick's direction (PadAxisUp ..., or up / down / left / right on \n343:- `input.padValues = []` †: each gamepad button's travel, 0 to 1 (the triggers; input.value reads them)\n335:- `input.names = null` †: the actions' names on the Controls screen ({ attack: 'Sword' }; false hides one from rebinding: the game's menu.controls); onBindings(b): called with the player's new bindings (the game save\n504:- `game.saves()` †: game.saves: the save slots (section 10k), made when first read\n627:- `new E.Saves(game, o) → saves` †: game.saves (made when first read): o is menu.saves ({ slots, version, migrate, write, read })\n639:- `saves.canSave = true` †: the pause menu offers Save (a JRPG turns it off away from save points)\n679:- `rig.drawPortrait(g, x, y, size = 40, o = {})` †: a close-up bust for dialog boxes and menus, drawn live from the rig (blinks, hair and hats included): rig.drawPortrait(g, x, y, 40, { zoom: 3, t\n1123:- `talk.say(text, o = {})`: open with one string or a list of strings (each starts a new page). opts: { name, onDone, choices, onChoice, portrait: rig (a live close-up of that Humanoid beside the\n# Engine modules\n\nA module is one general system in a small file of its own, `engine/modules/<name>.js`, loaded after the core\n(`engine/my-3d2dge.js`) and attached to `My3D2dge`. The core stays as it is; a game carries only the modules it uses.\nWhich system goes where, and the rules a kit and a module follow, are in `docs/KITS.md` (the genre plan's design rules,","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ea1b61d-e1b8-4350-be76-ae4a4cbc51a9","uuid":"14d04407-b139-4c27-984a-97bd85a2abed","timestam