sidearm, one shot, your hand in shot). In a burning cell or below 5 s left, it's the only option.\"\"\")\n\n# --- contracts\nrep(\"Kill Colonel Renn on the Customs House steps at the treaty signing in Port Clement. Long shot from the Fleet side with the Curate, or walk in on Authority papers with a bomb in a case. Then the town burns: scripted ignition at three points, militia both ways. Get out. Mr. Sunday's boat moves to the Fleet. Two more posts appear.\",\n    \"Kill Colonel Renn on the Customs House steps at the treaty signing in Port Clement. Sell hands you a worn Curate for a long shot from the old harbour wall, or walk in on Authority papers with a bomb in a case. Then the town burns: scripted ignition at three points, militia both ways. Get out. Mr. Sunday moves his stock to a hulk at the Fleet. Two more posts appear.\")\nrep(\"She supplies a Gardener. Burn Reed Camp from upwind.\", \"She supplies a worn Gardener (not an unlock). Burn Reed Camp from upwind.\")\nrep('\"This is the woman you came to kill.\" Read any 3 of 8 survey stakes (below). Then the road to the Sill opens on the map.', '\"This is the woman you came to kill.\" Read any 3 of 8 survey stakes (below; ones already found count). Then the road to the Sill opens on the map.')\n\n# --- shop\nrep(\"\"\"- **Mr. Sunday's boat:** a visit is a big, simple screen (section 11): his catalogue, one gun at a time. Buying unlocks that gun at every crate. He also sells camouflage cream (Stretch), throwables and repair kits? No: only guns and throwables. Keep it clean.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- **Mr. Sunday's boat:** a visit is a big, simple screen (section 11): his catalogue, one gun at a time. Buying unlocks that gun at every crate. He sells guns and throwables, nothing else.\"\"\")\n\n# --- screens\nrep(\"\"\"Mouse hover moves focus and click picks, on every menu; release pointer lock when one opens (`document.exitPointerLock()`) and capture again on the next click.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Mouse hover moves focus and click picks, on every menu; release pointer lock when one opens (`document.exitPointerLock()`) and capture again on the next click. In the world, the mouse aims and fires; on things your hands hold (map, logbook, Sunday's card, the watch dial), left click acts on what's under the pencil or cursor.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"**About / Credits (from pause and title).** Scrollable big text (`shell.show('help', { sections })`). Contents exactly as TASK.md lists: Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback, plus library credits (my-3D2dge MIT, three.js r182 MIT, Rapier 0.19.3 Apache-2.0, any CC0 store props used). Fill it from `exit-interview.json` in the build, so the two can't disagree. See section 15 for ordering.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"**About / Credits (from pause and title).** Big text in the engine's HTML shell: `const ui = new E.Shell(game, {})` keeps the standard menu, and `ui.show('help', { sections: [[heading, text], ...] })` shows it (VERIFIED with CSS zoom, mouse click and long text). Contents exactly as TASK.md lists: Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback, plus library credits (my-3D2dge MIT, three.js r182 MIT, Rapier 0.19.3 Apache-2.0, any CC0 store props used). Fill it from `exit-interview.json` via `window.__answers` (A1), so the two can't disagree. See section 15 for ordering. **Trap:** the Shell focuses Back, which scrolls the panel (`.esh-mod`) to the bottom. Set its `scrollTop = 0` after opening, and each step move `scrollTop` from the sticks and d-pad, so a controller can read the whole thing. Test it.\"\"\")\n\n# --- multiplayer\nrep(\"\"\"- Don't declare `hub:webgpu`; the game runs on either backend.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- Don't declare `hub:webgpu`; the game runs on either backend. If World3D can't start at all in a session, call `AIHub.fail(message)`.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"with `connect()` in an inline script straight after the client, no title world, and `ready()` before the warm-up, **all scenarios passed**\"\"\".replace(\"with `connect()`\", \"With `connect()`\"),\n    \"\"\"With `connect()` in an inline script straight after the client, no title world, and `ready()` before the warm-up, **all scenarios passed**\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"Appendix A6 has the exact order. Keep it that way as your boot grows, and test it (section 14).\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Appendix A1 and A6, followed literally on the kit, passed all five harness runs. Keep that order as your boot grows, and test it (section 14).\"\"\")\n\n# --- testing wording\nrep(\"\"\"12. Input: stub gamepad (A7's `add_init_script` pattern in Appendix A8) reads `R2`;\"\"\", \"\"\"12. Input: the stub gamepad in A8 reads `R2`;\"\"\")\n\n# --- coverage\nrep(\"\"\"| Performance unlimited, no FPS targets | Spend freely: raise `GRASS_R`, flame counts, soldiers. Don't optimise. |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"| Performance unlimited, no FPS targets | Spend freely: raise `GRASS_R`, flame counts, `lights`, `glowLights`, soldiers at each post. Don't optimise. |\"\"\")\n\n# --- A1: a real constant, not a placeholder that throws\nrep(\"\"\"const OUT = '../REPLACE-WITH-THE-NAME-TASK-MD-GIVES.html', E3 = resolve('engine');\"\"\", \"\"\"const OUT = '../REPLACE-WITH-THE-NAME-TASK-MD-GIVES.html', TITLE = 'YOUR TITLE', E3 = resolve('engine');\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"<title>${TITLE_FROM_YOUR_DATA}</title>\"\"\", \"\"\"<title>${TITLE}</title>\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"`TITLE_FROM_YOUR_DATA` is a constant you define. The session client must stay the first script after the charset, byte for byte: the hub replaces and checks it.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"VERIFIED as written (with those two constants filled in): 4.83 MB, boots from `file://`. The session client must stay the first script after the charset, byte for byte: the hub replaces and checks it.\"\"\")\n\n# --- A4: reversed smoothstep edges are undefined on real GPUs; use the safe form\nrep(\"\"\"const width = float(.46).mul(float(1).sub(yy)).mul(smoothstep(float(0), float(.16), yy).mul(.5).add(.5)), body = smoothstep(width, width.mul(.45), xx);\"\"\",\n\"\"\"const width = float(.46).mul(float(1).sub(yy)).mul(smoothstep(float(0), float(.16), yy).mul(.5).add(.5)), body = float(1).sub(smoothstep(width.mul(.45), width.add(.002), xx));\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"//   sm.colorNode = vec3(.09, .08, .075); sm.opacityNode = smoothstep(float(1), float(.15), rr).mul(attribute('fade','float')).mul(.5);  // rr: squared distance from the quad's centre, from uv\"\"\",\n\"\"\"//   sm.colorNode = vec3(.09, .08, .075); sm.opacityNode = float(1).sub(smoothstep(float(.15), float(1), rr)).mul(attribute('fade','float')).mul(.5);  // rr: squared distance from the quad's centre, from uv\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"// the flames: one merged mesh of quads in a boot step, MAX = 2400; TSL draws a licking teardrop from uv and time\nconst { attribute, uv, uniform, vec3, float, sin, smoothstep, mix, clamp } = E.TSL;\"\"\",\n\"\"\"// the flames: one merged mesh of quads in a boot step; TSL draws a licking teardrop from uv and time\nconst { attribute, uv, uniform, vec3, float, sin, smoothstep, mix, clamp } = E.TSL, MAX = 2400;\"\"\")\nopen(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nprint('edited')\nEOF\ngrep -n \"Notary\\|TITLE_FROM\\|\\? No:\\|A7's\" PLAN.md | head; cd .research/exp && python3 - <<'EOF'\ns = open('proto.js').read()\na = \"const body = smoothstep(width, width.mul(.45), x);\"\nassert a in s\ns = s.replace(a, \"const body = float(1).sub(smoothstep(width.mul(.45), width.add(.002), x));\")\nb = \"sm.opacityNode = smoothstep(float(1), float(.15), rr).mul(sf).mul(.5);\"\nassert b in s\ns = s.replace(b, \"sm.opacityNode = float(1).sub(smoothstep(float(.15), float(1), rr)).mul(sf).mul(.5);\")\nopen('proto.js','w').write(s)\nEOF\nnode build4.mjs && sed -i \"s/b = p.chromium.launch(args=\\['--enable-unsafe-webgpu','--enable-features=Vulkan','--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader'\\])/b = p.chromium.launch()/\" run7.py && timeout 280 python3 run7.py | tail -6 && timeout 280 python3 run10.py | tail -3","description":"Apply plan fixes and re-verify the safer flame shader on both backends","timeout":590000}}}
