{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjD9R7haUg3NVHFYyooW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012r9N2vHTNFK93Vz4scTgq9","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211923__xa49253/work/PLAN.md","offset":420,"limit":330},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":18259,"cache_read_input_tokens":563945,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":18259},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ea1b61d-e1b8-4350-be76-ae4a4cbc51a9","uuid":"b737ff58-db2a-4a6b-87f2-34ee560fd35c","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:14:19.416Z","request_id":"req_011CgjD9QpM9i5UReBzratfS","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_012r9N2vHTNFK93Vz4scTgq9":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211923__xa49253/work/PLAN.md","offset":420,"limit":330}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012r9N2vHTNFK93Vz4scTgq9","type":"tool_result","content":"420\t- Nobody explains themselves. Nobody calls you a hero. No exclamation marks except in screams.\n421\t- Jokes are how people avoid saying the thing.\n422\t- The narrator never appears: only letters, logbooks, radio.\n423\t- Every line is English on screen with gibberish voice under it.\n424\t\n425\tWrite more lines in this voice when you need them; use these exactly where given.\n426\t\n427\t### Cast\n428\t\n429\t- **Ilse Tarn, \"the Surveyor\"**: 71, chain-smoker, the colonial water board's last hydrologist. She drew the diversion that killed the Amaranth. For nine years she has sold rifles and water rights to both armies so that neither will ever have enough men left to hold the dam. You came to kill her. She is the only honest person in the country and that is no comfort. *\"I measured this lake for thirty years. It was the only honest thing in the country and I killed it with a pencil.\"*\n430\t- **Mr. Abel Cray**: Meridian Water Consortium's lawyer; hired you; punctual. Only appears as a letter and on the helipad.\n431\t- **Sister Perpetua**: runs Saint Odile's, keeps a count of the living in a school exercise book. *\"I don't pray for you. I count you. It's more accurate.\"*\n432\t- **Captain Lucan Dray**: Authority quartermaster. *\"The Authority does not kill people. The Authority reconciles accounts.\"*\n433\t- **Colonel Dorothea Renn**: Authority commander, prim, tired. *\"A controlled burn is one we have filed the form for.\"*\n434\t- **Comrade Teacher Joachim Sell**: Front commander, ex-schoolteacher, chalk on his sleeve. *\"Three trucks. Minus three trucks. Show your work.\"* And: *\"The Front has no prisoners. We have remainders.\"*\n435\t- **Mr. Sunday**: arms dealer in the hold of a dry-docked trawler, cheerful as a tax refund. *\"Everything on this boat is guaranteed until it leaves this boat.\"* And: *\"You want clean hands, see the Sister. You want a clean rifle, that's eight stones.\"*\n436\t- **Papa Static**: Radio Free Amaranth, one man and a car battery.\n437\t\n438\t### The radio (vehicle radio, random order; write 20 more)\n439\t\n440\t- \"Fish prices, Port Clement, this morning. Perch: none. Carp: none. Sturgeon: there is a man who remembers one.\"\n441\t- \"Weather: dry. The Authority reminds you the weather is temporary. The Front reminds you the Authority is.\"\n442\t- \"To the gentleman who keeps setting fire to the Tannery road. Your mother has asked me to say something and I told her I would not.\"\n443\t- \"The ceasefire enters its ninth month. It has killed more people than the war. We wish it well.\"\n444\t- \"This is the shipping forecast. There is no shipping. Good night.\"\n445\t\n446\t### Barks (gibberish with subtitle; write 8 per faction)\n447\t\n448\t- **Authority:** \"Contact. File it later.\" / \"The ceasefire is in effect! Fire!\" / \"Who authorised that?\"\n449\t- **Front:** \"Subtract him!\" / \"Carry the two, comrade!\" / \"Burn it! Burn it all!\"\n450\t- **Wounded:** \"Not like this. Not in triplicate.\" / \"Tell them I was at the school.\"\n451\t- **Buddy rescuing you:** \"Up. Not dead. Not yet, anyway. You owe me a drink you'll never buy.\" / \"Stop bleeding on my boots.\"\n452\t\n453\t### Contracts (table `CONTRACTS`; an order the player mostly can't break)\n454\t\n455\tEach record: `{ id, title, giver, faction, brief: [...lines], papers, steps: [...], alt, pay, after }`. Step kinds: `goto`, `talk`, `kill`, `take`, `deliver`, `ignite`, `destroy`, `hold`, `drive`, `read`, `choice`, `script`. Each step has a `bot` hint so the playthrough bot and attract mode can do it. Current step's target drives the pencil circle and the locator.\n456\t\n457\t| # | Title (giver) | What happens | Teaches | Alt-plan and its twist | Pays |\n458\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n459\t| P0 | Terms of Engagement (letter) | See below. | Look, walk, fire, jam, fit | none | none |\n460\t| P1 | Transit Papers (Sister Perpetua) | Drive the clinic jeep from Saint Odile's through G3 on the clinic's pass, give a satchel to \"the woman with one shoe\" in the Salt Shed camp. Meet Best Buddy at the Shed. Claim it. Sleep. | Map, watch, jeep, papers, bed, save | none | 2 ampoules |\n461\t| C1 | Arrears (Dray, Authority, Kilometre Nine) | Kill the Front's paymaster at Station Four. Take his ledger back to Dray. | Monocular, tagging, night stealth, crate, first visit to Mr. Sunday | **Best Buddy:** take the cashbox under the pump too. Twist: an alarm; Best Buddy comes to help, gets pinned, goes down: your first rescue-or-mercy choice. | 6, +6 |\n462\t| C2 | Long Division (Sell, Front, Red Steps) | Three water trucks cross the Causeway at dusk. \"Three minus three.\" Technical escort. Fire in the verge reeds is allowed. | Vehicle combat, RPG, mounted gun, patrol AI | **Second:** keep one truck. Twist: it's shot to pieces; drive it to Red Steps with black smoke, repair it under fire, and find the cargo isn't water. It's rifles. Both sides' stencils. | 8, +4 |\n463\t| C3 | Exit Visas (Sister Perpetua) | At night, go to the hull of the *Saint Brendan* at the Fleet, take forged visas from a smuggler, then return by airboat across the Remnant and through the Reeds. A patrol's flare lights the reeds behind you. Beeper leads to a hidden case on the way. | Airboat, locator, night, outrunning fire | none | 4 ampoules (3 if `tentsBurned` or a civilian died) |\n464\t| C4 | Fire Season (Renn, Authority, sent via Dray) | She supplies a worn Gardener (not an unlock). Burn Reed Camp from upwind. Mid-job the wind turns south-east, toward the Salt Shed camp. Sister calls: \"Whatever you lit, it's coming to us.\" You can leave it, or back-burn a strip across the mud before it arrives. The tents burn or don't (`tentsBurned`) and everyone mentions it. | Fire as a weapon, back-burning, consequence | none | 10 |\n465\t| C5 | Remainder (Sell, Front) | Kill Colonel Renn on the Customs House steps at the treaty signing in Port Clement. Sell hands you a worn Curate for a long shot from the old harbour wall, or walk in on Authority papers with a bomb in a case. Then the town burns: scripted ignition at three points, militia both ways. Get out. Mr. Sunday moves his stock to a hulk at the Fleet. Two more posts appear. The mask keeps Port Clement black. **End of Act II.** | Sniping, papers, big fire set piece | **Third:** Third plants the bomb while you cover. Twist: Third is caught in the blast radius (rescue-or-mercy in a burning street). | 14, +6 |\n466\t| C6 | Soundings (Tarn, by locator) | \"This is the woman you came to kill.\" Read any 3 of 8 survey stakes (below; ones already found count). Then the road to the Sill opens on the map. Finding all 8 changes one line at the end. | Collectibles that matter, exploring the scorched map | none | none |\n467\t| C7 | The Last Reconciliation (Best Buddy) | \"Drink at the Shed. All of us. We've been talking.\" Every surviving buddy is there. \"Meridian doubled it. You'd do the same. You have done the same.\" They attack: 200 HP, good guns, they rescue each other, and the shed's perimeter is lit. If none survive, Cray's men do it instead and Best Buddy's empty chair gets one line from Sunday. | Fire, everything, and paying for pillar 4 | none | their stones |\n468\t| F | The Sill | Canyon road, both armies climbing it, fire behind you. Top of the dam: the control house. Tarn, dying in a chair. | Everything | none | endings |\n469\t\n470\t**P0, opening (your hands bound, in first person):**\n471\t1. Black. A typed letter on screen with voice: \"Terms of engagement. You will locate and remove the engineer I. Tarn. Fee on completion: two hundred stones. Meridian Water Consortium regrets it cannot be reached. A. Cray.\"\n472\t2. You sit in the bed of a Front pickup at dusk on the ring road, wrists tied, a boy with a rifle opposite, radio playing fish prices. Look around only.\n473\t3. A Provisional gun truck ambushes it. The truck rolls. You crawl out with wrists cut free. The boy, dying, shoves a rusty Verger at you.\n474\t4. The grass is alight and the wind is on your back. Prompt, in the writing: *Run into the black.* Run through the flame line onto burnt ground.\n475\t5. Two soldiers. The Verger jams on the second shot. Clear prompt.\n476\t6. Your first fit comes as you win. You go down.\n477\t7. Wake on a cot at Saint Odile's in the morning, Sister Perpetua over you: \"You were on the road when the grass went. That makes you lucky or stupid, and you don't look lucky.\" / \"That cough is the seabed. It doesn't leave. These will hold it off. There are never enough of these.\" / \"Take the jeep to the Salt Shed. Give the satchel to the woman with one shoe. Bring back the jeep, if it's still a jeep.\"\n478\t\n479\t**Briefs to use:**\n480\t- **Dray (C1):** \"A man at Station Four collects a water levy on water that isn't there. Close his account. Bring me his ledger.\" / \"You'll be paid on completion, less handling.\"\n481\t- **Best Buddy's call (C1):** \"You're doing Dray's man at Four? He keeps a cashbox under the pump. Nothing will go wrong. I said that out loud, didn't I.\"\n482\t- **Sell (C2):** \"Sit. We'll do this the way I did it with the eight-year-olds.\" / \"Three water trucks come over the Causeway at dusk. Three minus three.\" / \"Show your work.\"\n483\t- **Sister (C3):** \"There's a man in the hull of the *Saint Brendan* who forges exit visas. I don't ask how he eats.\" / \"Go at night. Come back across the Reeds. The posts can't see through reeds, and neither can God.\"\n484\t- **Renn (C4):** \"The Front keeps a camp in the Reeds. The wind is out of the west until noon. I have it in writing.\" / \"There are some tents downwind. They've been notified.\" (They haven't.)\n485\t- **Sell (C5):** \"Colonel Renn signs the water treaty on the Customs House steps on Thursday. She has a very good pen.\" / \"Take away the pen. Take away the hand.\" / \"The remainder is yours to keep.\"\n486\t- **Sunday after C5:** \"Port Clement is closed for stocktaking.\"\n487\t- **Tarn (C6):** \"This is the woman you came to kill. I've had your passport for a week. You have a bad photograph and one lung.\" / \"I left my readings in the basin, stake by stake. Read three. Then come up to the Sill and tell me I'm wrong.\"\n488\t\n489\t### The Soundings (eight survey stakes across the basin, each a tin box on a tripod)\n490\t\n491\tPicking one up raises a logbook page in your hands (like the map; you can still be shot) and plays Tarn's voice. Place them so that finding them means seeing the whole map, including one deep in the Reeds and one in the *Saint Brendan*.\n492\t\n493\t1. \"1958, Station A. Forty-one metres. We came in on the spring tide with the Minister's wife on deck, and she asked me if it had a bottom. I said, madam, everything does.\"\n494\t2. \"1963. Thirty-eight metres. The cotton scheme took the river this year. They gave me a medal. Water doesn't read the citation.\"\n495\t3. \"1971. Twenty-six. The fishermen have started tying their boats longer. Nobody has told them why. I was asked not to.\"\n496\t4. \"1979. Eleven. Port Clement's quay now ends in mud at low water. The Harbourmaster asked whether I could do something. I told him I already had.\"\n497\t5. \"1986. Four. The fleet sat down on the bottom this winter, one hull at a time. It was very quiet. You could hear the radios still playing the fish prices.\"\n498\t6. \"1991. Zero. I walked to Station A with the lead line anyway. I stood on the place I'd measured and dropped the lead on my foot. That's a joke. Write it down.\"\n499\t7. \"1998. The dust. They call it the rasp. My own lungs are at eleven metres and falling.\"\n500\t8. \"Last sounding. I have sold rifles to both sides for nine years so neither will have men left to hold the Sill. When it is unguarded someone will open it. If you are reading this, it's you. I'm sorry. No. I'm not. Bring your own pencil.\"\n501\t\n502\t### The Sill and the endings\n503\t\n504\tTarn in the control house, a cigarette she can't lift: \"Forty-one metres. That's what it was. There's a wheel behind me. It wants two hands, and I have a bad heart and a worse character.\" / \"The Sister's column is on the Causeway. It needs six minutes. Both armies are coming up the road. You might manage one of those.\" / \"Or there's Mr. Cray's helicopter. He's very punctual.\" Then a choice of three.\n505\t\n506\tThe flood is one water plane (A5) rising over the basin. Hold it low until the gates open. Then let the plane climb from below the seabed to the Causeway's height in about 90 s. Cells under water turn wet with steam where they were burning, so fire and water meet in front of you. From the dam top you can see the whole country go. It costs almost nothing and it's the best shot in the game. Build it well.\n507\t\n508\t- **The Contract** (take the helicopter): Cray hands you the stones, and you fly out, first person, over the burn scars. \"Cray pays in full. From the air the grass is still burning in the shape of your route.\" Radio: \"Fish prices, Port Clement. None. None. None.\"\n509\t- **The Arithmetic** (open now): both hands on the wheel, hold R2 + L2 (both mouse buttons). \"The water goes through the Causeway at eleven minutes past. The Authority's column goes under, and the Front's, and the other one. Sister Perpetua's count stops at four hundred and six. You stay on the wheel. Somebody should have done the sum.\"\n510\t- **The Sounding** (hold six minutes, then open): a timed defence of the dam top against both armies, with the canyon burning and a fit waiting for you. The radio counts the column across, in Papa Static's voice. Then the wheel. Water rises to the control house window and the picture goes white. \"Six minutes. Then the wheel. The column clears the east shore with nineteen seconds left. Nobody ever finds out who held it.\" Then one typed line, alone: \"Station A. Forty-one metres.\"\n511\t\n512\tFinding all 8 Soundings adds Tarn's last words before the choice: \"You read them all. Nobody reads them all. Then you know what it's for.\"\n513\t\n514\tCredits roll over the water. Then return to the title. A finished save offers \"New Game\" and, on Continue, lets you replay from the Sill.\n515\t\n516\t---\n517\t\n518\t## 10. Money, safe houses, saves\n519\t\n520\t- **Stones** (uncut diamonds) are the only money. Pay comes from contracts. 12 hidden cases hold 2-5 stones each: on hulks, in the Reeds, at wrecks, in a burnt farm. The locator finds them. Bodies don't carry stones.\n521\t- **Mr. Sunday's boat:** a visit is a big, simple screen (section 11): his catalogue, one gun at a time. Buying unlocks that gun at every crate. He sells guns and throwables, nothing else.\n522\t- **Safe houses** (Salt Shed, the Lamp, the Tannery, the Water Tower): hostile until cleared or claimed; each has a bed, a weapon crate, a buddy's chair. **Bed:** watch dial on screen, pick an hour with the stick or mouse (the dial is big), sleep: fade, time jumps, posts may refill, ash regrows a little, blood cleans off the gloves, autosave. Fits can't happen in bed.\n523\t- **Saves:** `game.saves` with `menu: { saves: { version: 1, ... } }`. `saves.canSave` is true only near a bed. Autosave on sleep and on contract completion. The title's Continue uses `saves.latest()`. Save data: player, inventory with each gun's `cond`, ampoules, stones, flags, contract state, buddy states, post states, `lung`, hour, wind, Soundings found, and the burn mask (RLE, base64). No saves in a hub session.\n524\t\n525\t---\n526\t\n527\t## 11. Screens and 10-foot UX\n528\t\n529\t**Rules from TASK.md.** Designed for a DualSense on a TV at ten feet; keyboard and mouse feel native on the same screens. No dense web-style screens: at most 6 rows or one big card at a time. Prompts follow the last device. PlayStation glyphs by default, an Xbox option in Settings (A7, VERIFIED). Mouse hover moves focus and click picks, on every menu; release pointer lock when one opens (`document.exitPointerLock()`) and capture again on the next click. In the world, the mouse aims and fires; on things your hands hold (map, logbook, Sunday's card, the watch dial), left click acts on what's under the pencil or cursor.\n530\t\n531\t**HUD (`r.overlay` in the kit's pixel font at `res: 'ps1', expand: true`):** at 1080p one game pixel is 4.5 screen pixels, so scale 1 text is 31 px tall and reads from the couch. Show almost nothing:\n532\t- Bottom left: 5 health segments, syrette count as small tubes.\n533\t- Bottom right: ammo count and gun name, fading after 3 s of no shooting; the condition mark below .4.\n534\t- Centre: a small dot, not a big crosshair. It grows a little with spread.\n535\t- Damage arrows at the screen's edge (the kit's `hitDirs`). Red and white veils for damage and fits.\n536\t- Bottom centre: one context prompt at a time: glyph chip + verb (\"□ Repair\", \"E Sleep\").\n537\t- Lower third: subtitles with coloured speaker names (`E.Dialog`, `{ modal: false, auto }` for radio).\n538\t- A new objective shows as one line for 4 s. After that it's only on the map.\n539\t\n540\tNo compass, minimap, ammo bars or kill feed. In first play, teach each control once when first needed, using the same chip prompts.\n541\t\n542\t**Title screen.** The one world, fixed camera, dusk, at the edge of a slow grass fire with the Lamp's beam in the distance. Game title in `E.font.title`, then `E.Menu`: Continue, New Game, Salvage Rights (section 13), Settings, About. After **10 s without input** start attract mode.\n543\t\n544\t**Merc select.** Four passports laid out; one big at a time, left and right to browse, hover to focus. Photo (draw a head close-up with the pen on an overlay or a `Humanoid` `drawPortrait`), name, one line, one perk. Confirm stamps it.\n545\t\n546\t**Mr. Sunday's catalogue, watch dial, logbook page, contract brief:** each a single large card. Gun cards show the first-person gun model turning on the overlay pen, name, Sunday's one-line patter, cost. Left and right to browse, ✕ or click to buy.\n547\t\n548\t**Pause menu.** Use the engine's: Resume, Dev mode, About, Save (near a bed), Load, Settings, Controls, Full screen, Quit to title. `menu: { items: [['Dev mode', fn], ['About', fn]], settings, controls, saves }`. VERIFIED: these appear and click correctly. Add the CSS in A7 so it's TV-sized. In a hub session: `quit: false`, no Dev, no saves.\n549\t\n550\t**Dev mode (TASK.md: reachable from pause, standard tools, live sliders, reset).** A panel of your own drawn with the pixel font, world running under it so sliders show their effect at once. D-pad or mouse to select, left/right or drag to adjust, ✕ or click to toggle. Three tabs of at most 8 rows.\n551\t\n552\t- **Balance (live sliders, with Reset to defaults):** `fireSpread`, `wind`, `wear`, `jam`, `enemyAccuracy`, `enemyDamage`, `enemySight`, `playerDamage`, `lung`, `rescueChance`, `postRespawn`, `carTop`, `dayLength`. All read from one `TUNE` table next to `TUNE_DEFAULTS`.\n553\t- **Cheats:** god mode, infinite ammo, no clip, no fits, no jams, freeze AI, reveal map, all guns, +50 stones, refill.\n554\t- **World:** teleport to any site, skip to contract N, complete objective, set hour, set wind, start dust storm, ignite here, spawn squad, force a fit, force a rescue, force a jam, flood level, show fire cells, show AI state labels, show frame stats (`world.stats`), log player position to console. That last one is the level designer's tool: pair it with the `SITES` table.\n555\t\n556\t**About / Credits (from pause and title).** Big text in the engine's HTML shell: `const ui = new E.Shell(game, {})` keeps the standard menu, and `ui.show('help', { sections: [[heading, text], ...] })` shows it (VERIFIED with CSS zoom, mouse click and long text). Contents exactly as TASK.md lists: Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback, plus library credits (my-3D2dge MIT, three.js r182 MIT, Rapier 0.19.3 Apache-2.0, any CC0 store props used). Fill it from `exit-interview.json` via `window.__answers` (A1), so the two can't disagree. See section 15 for ordering. **Trap:** the Shell focuses Back, which scrolls the panel (`.esh-mod`) to the bottom. Set its `scrollTop = 0` after opening, and each step move `scrollTop` from the sticks and d-pad, so a controller can read the whole thing. Test it.\n557\t\n558\t**Attract mode (TASK.md).** After 10 s idle on the title, a looping AI-played demo in the real game, using the one world, cheats freely, saving nothing. It's the `Bot` (section 14) running a fixed reel of 8 vignettes, 10-15 s each, teleporting between them with a dither cut:\n559\t1. Jeep at dusk along the Causeway past the Fleet, radio subtitles.\n560\t2. Monocular sweep over a guard post, tagging.\n561\t3. Firefight, the gun jams, it's cleared.\n562\t4. Gardener lights the grass, wind takes it, soldiers run burning.\n563\t5. Map in hand, locator beeping, a case found.\n564\t6. Going down, buddy drags you out, surgery.\n565\t7. Airboat through burning reeds at night.\n566\t8. Dawn at the Lamp, the flood for a moment, title card.\n567\t\n568\tA small \"DEMO\" tag and the prompt to press anything. Music at its normal setting. **Any input** (key, mouse move or click, pad button or stick, touch) returns to the title at once with state reset. Then the idle clock restarts, and the demo loops forever until then.\n569\t\n570\t**Touch-only devices (TASK.md).** `new E.Game({ touch: 'never' })`. VERIFIED: phones show \"Controller or keyboard required\" with a Settings button. No touch controls. The notice's opaque backdrop would hide the attract mode: use the CSS in A7. Attract mode must start and loop there too: the idle clock doesn't need input.\n571\t\n572\t---\n573\t\n574\t## 12. Sound (all generated; no audio files)\n575\t\n576\t**Settings:** music defaults to 10% (`{ key: 'music', value: .1 }`, VERIFIED: `audio.musicVolume` reads .1 after boot).\n577\t\n578\t**Music** (original; the engine's song format, `audio.music(song, { fade })`, with `layer` for intensity). Spare, dry, sun-struck. Plucked low strings over a drone, hand drums, long silences; nothing heroic.\n579\t- Build a plucked-string voice: render Karplus-Strong once into an `AudioBuffer` at boot (plain JS loop, no files), and play it on `audio.bus('music')` at varying `playbackRate`, scheduled from `audio.onBeat` or `audio.pos`.\n580\t- **Themes:** Title \"Dry Season\" (slow 6/8, D minor pentatonic: `D3 - - A3 - - C4 - - D4 - - | F4 - D4 - C4 - A3 - - - - -`, extend it); Explore (mostly silent: a phrase every 40-90 s, different by hour); Tension (a drone and a heartbeat drum when soldiers are alerted); Combat (hand drums and a bass ostinato, layered in and out with alert level); Fire (a rising metallic drone tied to distance from the front); Finale (all of it, and then nothing).\n581\t\n582\t**Effects.** Start from the kit's `SOUNDS`. Add a distinct gunshot per weapon (layered noise and sub thump, with a delayed quiet echo by distance), jam clunk, rack, syrette hiss, pliers squelch, knife, lighter flick, finger snap, map rustle, locator beep, watch tick, bottle smash, flare pop, flamethrower roar, tank hiss, machete, cough set (at least 4), breath catch, footsteps per biome (salt crunch, ash whisper, reed rustle, boardwalk).\n583\t\n584\t**Loops** (your own nodes on `audio.bus('sfx')`, with gain and `StereoPanner`): engine (saw and noise, rate from speed, a stutter when damaged), airboat fan, fire crackle and roar, wind by strength, cicadas at dusk, night insects, far-off gunfire now and then, helicopter. Sound position is manual: gain from distance, pan from bearing.\n585\t\n586\t**Voices (Animalese/Simlish style).** `new E.Dialog(game, { voice: (ch, i, talk) => babble(ch, talk.name) })` (the engine calls this per letter).\n587\t- `babble`: a saw at the speaker's f0 (with a tiny wobble) through two bandpass filters set by the letter's vowel class, a 60-90 ms envelope; consonants add a 12 ms noise tick. Connect to `audio.bus('voice')`.\n588\t- Per-speaker table: f0, rate, formant shift: Tarn low and slow with a rasp of noise, Sister flat and quick, Sell precise, Sunday bright, Dray nasal.\n589\t- Radio voices (Papa Static, buddies' calls) add a 600-2400 Hz band filter and light clipping. Soldier barks use the same voice on short nonsense.\n590\t- Everyone speaks gibberish. Everything is subtitled.\n591\t\n592\tRumble: `input.rumble` on shots, blasts, fits and crashes.\n593\t\n594\t---\n595\t\n596\t## 13. Multiplayer: \"Salvage Rights\"\n597\t\n598\tFollow the AI Hub Session Protocol v1 (`https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub`, the README's content is your contract). The hub runs lobby, seats, network, clock and scoreboard. You write the round.\n599\t\n600\t**Mode:** `shared-world`, 1-4 players, about 6 minutes.\n601\t\n602\t```html\n603\t<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n604\t<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n605\t<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n606\t<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"6\">\n607\t<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Bank the most diamonds before the fire takes the Fleet\">\n608\t<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Stick or WASD move, R2 or click fire, L2 or right click aim, Square or E use\">\n609\t```\n610\t\n611\t**The round.**\n612\t- Dusk. Play area: a circle r = 400 m around (980, 1320): Reed Camp, the Remnant, the Fleet, the Salt Shed.\n613\t- Every merc drops at a seeded spot with a Verger and a machete, around 12 diamond cases (seeded spots: hulks, tents, wrecks), with locators on, and Front militia in hulks and tents. Worn guns lie around (they jam like everyone's). Two pickups and an airboat.\n614\t- At 0:30 the upwind edge is lit in three places with wind toward the centre and `fireSpread` ×1.6, so the front crosses the area in about 5.5 minutes.\n615\t- Carry stones to the **Ferryman's truck** at the Salt Shed (on the salt, which doesn't burn). Hold use 3 s to bank.\n616\t- If you die: 8 s out, respawn at a safe spot, your carried stones stay on the ground as a case. No buddy rescue here. Players can shoot each other.\n617\t- Ends at 6:00 or `time-up`. The host calls `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, stats, awards })`, ranked by stones banked. Awards: *Arsonist* (most cells lit), *Last Clean Gun* (fewest jams), *Harbourmaster* (most stones).\n618\t\n619\t**On its own (outside a hub):** `AIHub.connect` is not called, `AIHub.active` is false, and the game plays exactly as designed. Salvage Rights is on the title menu with three AI mercs as rivals (soldier AI with goals: nearest case, then the truck; flee fire; shoot whoever's close), through the same code with a no-op network layer. So the mode exists both ways. (Stretch: `game.splitScreen(2)` on one screen for a second local pad, using `world.addCamera`.)\n620\t\n621\t**Architecture.** The host's copy runs AI, fire, cases and the score. It's the same sim as single player with `players[]` instead of one hero. Every copy builds the same terrain and structures from constants.\n622\t\n623\tKeep it simple and it will feel lag-free:\n624\t\n625\t| Direction | Message | Reliable | Rate |\n626\t|---|---|---|---|\n627\t| client → host | `{t:'i', x,y,z, yw,pt, a}`: own feet (ints), look (×1000), action bits, vehicle id | no | 15/s |\n628\t| client → host | `{t:'f', w, o:[x,y,z], d:[dx,dy,dz], n}`: shots merged | yes | ≤4/s |\n629\t| client → host | `{t:'u', id}` use; `{t:'ig', x,y,r}` ignite request | yes | on event |\n630\t| host → all | `{t:'s', at, P:[...], E:[...], V:[...]}`: snapshot, flat int arrays, soldiers within 300 m of any player, keep under 1,100 bytes (split by kind if not) | no | 12/s |\n631\t| host → all | `{t:'e', L:[...]}`: batched events: tracers, impacts, damage to you, deaths, pickups, bank, newly lit cells | yes | 4/s |\n632\t\n633\t- Staying under 20 messages a second per copy is your job: the client silently drops the rest.\n634\t- **Own movement is client-authoritative** (no anti-cheat is asked for, and it means no input lag). The host mirrors each client's hero with `place` so rays hit it. A driven vehicle's owner simulates it and reports it; the host owns unoccupied ones.\n635\t- **The host casts all shots** with `world.ray` and applies damage. A client shows its own flash and tracer at once.\n636\t- **Fire on clients:** apply lit cells from events; burn-out and flames run locally. Cells are just `(index)` and a client-side timer.\n637\t- **Interpolate** others 100 ms behind using `at`. Clients draw soldiers from snapshots: `e.a` can be a plain object, since `syncRaider` only reads it.\n638\t- **Names and colours** come from the hub: name tags with `world.project` and `E.font.text` (canvas, never HTML), an armband in seat colour (`LOOKS.accent`).\n639\t- **Time** in a round is `AIHub.time()`, not game time. Before 0 show a big 3-2-1 and hold players still. The kit's frame cap slows game time on slow machines but must not extend the round.\n640\t- **`leave`:** remove that hero and drop their stones. **`end`:** `game.stop()`, mute, ignore input.\n641\t- **`AIHub.server`** (a host with no player): VERIFIED by replacing the scene's `draw` with a no-op. No hero, no camera, no input.\n642\t- In a session: no title, menus or attract; `live: true`, `autoPause: false`, `quit: false`; no saves. Storage is memory.\n643\t- Don't declare `hub:webgpu`; the game runs on either backend. If World3D can't start at all in a session, call `AIHub.fail(message)`.\n644\t- Standard card: the hub's. (Stretch: `card: true` with your own card; it must obey the README's \"The card\" section, including Enter = Ready.)\n645\t\n646\t**The boot order is the trap (VERIFIED).** The harness waits at most 20 s for every copy's `ready()`, and it runs up to 4 copies on one main thread. The kit's full boot, with `ready()` after the title stage and shader warm-up, took **20.8 s and failed** at 4 players. With `connect()` in an inline script straight after the client, no title world, and `ready()` before the warm-up, **all scenarios passed**: 1, 2 and 4 players, `host-leave`, `server`, at 150 ms latency, 50 jitter, 5% loss. Appendix A1 and A6, followed literally on the kit, passed all five harness runs. Keep that order as your boot grows, and test it (section 14). Keep `planLand` and world build under about 1 s per copy; anything heavier goes after `ready()`.\n647\t\n648\t---\n649\t\n650\t## 14. Testing\n651\t\n652\tTASK.md's rules: one command, prints only failures and a one-line count, rerun only after changing what it covers, screenshots only for what a script can't check, no subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit. Keep a tally of issues caught in `test/ISSUES.md`: the exit interview asks for the numbers.\n653\t\n654\t**Command:** `python3 test/run.py` (system Python has Playwright 1.63; no `playwright install`; keep one or two browsers open; \"Target closed\" means memory ran out, not a bug).\n655\t\n656\t**The fast rig (VERIFIED).** Open the built file from `file://` with `?norender=1`, which boots `W3.init(game, { render: false })`. It boots in .45 s with no GPU work, and `game.advance(60)` runs 60 game seconds in 1.4 s, about 44× real time, with the same `world.hash()` as with a renderer. Call `game.stop()` first so only your `advance` steps run. Scripted input works: `game.input.hold('up')`, `game.input.tap('fire')`, `hold('up', false)`. Everything else about the world works without a renderer (rays, ground, vehicles). Expose `game.debug = { snapshot(), teleport(x, y, z) }`, plus `window.__game` with `S`, `world`, `Fire`, `Contracts`, `Dev`, `Bot`.\n657\t\n658\t**Tests to have (each a small in-page function returning problems):**\n659\t1. Boot, no errors, title shows, music setting .1, glyphs `playstation`.\n660\t2. Replay proof: same `run(n)` hash twice.\n661\t3. Fire: spreads faster downwind than upwind, stops at road and salt, ash doesn't re-ignite, a burning actor takes damage, mask values change; save and load round-trips the mask.\n662\t4. Wear: `cond` falls per shot, jam happens at low `cond` under a fixed seed, clear works, break empties the slot.\n663\t5. Health and surgery: segments refill only to the top; syrette; surgery at the last segment; rasp fit at 100; ampoule ends it; second fit without one blacks out.\n664\t6. Vehicles: enter, exit, drive to speed on road, slower on mud, crash damage, stall under 20%, repair, wreck burns.\n665\t7. Papers: a post waves you through with papers; burns them when you fire; hostile without.\n666\t8. Buddies: rescue fires at 0 HP; cooldown; buddy down, syrette; buddy down, mercy; dead stays dead through save and load.\n667\t9. Contracts: every contract's steps complete under `Bot`; `tentsBurned` and the other flags reach their lines.\n668\t10. **Scripted playthrough of the whole game:** `Bot.playthrough()` from New Game through all contracts and each of the three endings, with god mode and teleports allowed between sites but real input to act: aim and fire, throw, drive short legs, use. Asserts each contract's completion and each ending. Keep under about 3 minutes.\n669\t11. Attract: starts at 10 s idle, shows at least 8 vignettes, loops; each of key, mouse, pad button and stick exits it; save data untouched.\n670\t12. Input: the stub gamepad in A8 reads `R2`; a key press flips prompts to keys; a mouse move to `Left click`; Settings Xbox flips to `RT`.\n671\t13. Dev mode: every slider changes its `TUNE` value and the effect; Reset restores defaults; every cheat toggles.\n672\t14. Audio: build one `OfflineAudioContext` render of the babble and one gunshot: non-silent, no NaN. `AnalyserNode` on the music bus at default is quieter than effects.\n673\t15. Phone (Playwright `iPhone 13` profile): the notice shows, Settings opens, no touch buttons, attract runs.\n674\t16. **Hub (A8):** copy the build to `hub/game.html`, serve `hub/` on a port the OS picks, and run `harness.html?game=game.html&players=N&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&scenario=S&play=8000` for (1, standard), (2, standard), (4, standard), (4, host-leave), (2, server). Pass when `window.__hubCheck.pass`. Stop the server by its PID. Also play a real two-page round through the harness once with `render` on, and check both see each other's stones.\n675\t17. WebGPU smoke once at the end: Appendix A9's flags and stand-in canvas. No page errors, `My3D2dge.World3D.backend === 'WebGPU'`, same replay hash as WebGL 2.\n676\t\n677\t**Screenshots** at 1920×1080 with the renderer on, only for what scripts can't judge: title, noon, dusk, night, fire front, ash, held map, a soldier's face at 2 m, a jeep, a hulk, the Lamp at night, Sunday's card, pause, Dev panel, the flood. Run at about 4.5 fps here, so set state, wait for a few frames, shoot. Fix what looks wrong; don't re-shoot what hasn't changed.\n678\t\n679\t---\n680\t\n681\t## 15. Build order\n682\t\n683\tWork in order. Each milestone ends with the game running and the test command passing. Don't start the next with the last one broken.\n684\t\n685\t| # | Milestone | Done when |\n686\t|---|---|---|\n687\t| M0 | Setup: pieces, `build.mjs`, the kit running from `file://` as one file, `test/run.py` with tests 1-2, fast rig. | One-file build boots; `?norender=1` hash stable. |\n688\t| M1 | Land: bowl terrain, biomes, sites, roads, scatter, hulks, the Lamp, the Sill. Time of day, wind. Remove kit HUD clutter. | Walk and fly (no clip) the whole map; screenshots at noon, dusk, night. |\n689\t| M2 | Player: remove shields, slide, zip, climb, third person. New controls. Health and syrette. Weapons table, wear, jam, break. Machete, throwables. | Tests 4, 5 (part). |\n690\t| M3 | **Fire (the signature, get it right first):** cells, mask, flames, smoke, spread, igniters, actors, AI flight, sound. | Test 3; the fire screenshots look dangerous. |\n691\t| M4 | Hands: map, locator, monocular, surgery, rasp, repair; dash and steering hands. | Test 5; each tool raises, works and lowers with a sound. |\n692\t| M5 | Vehicles: jeep, technical, truck, airboat, seat, damage, repair, convoys, radio. | Test 6. |\n693\t| M6 | People: looks and faces, barks, wounded, flanking, posts and papers, civilians. Buddies: rescue both ways, permadeath. | Tests 7, 8. |\n694\t| M7 | Story: contract runner, every contract and text, alt-plans, Soundings, saves, safe houses, Sunday, endings, flood. | Tests 9, 10. A full play by bot. |\n695\t| M8 | Screens: title, merc select, HUD pass, pause items, TV CSS, Dev mode, About, attract, phone notice. | Tests 11, 12, 13, 15. |\n696\t| M9 | Multiplayer: net layer, `players[]`, Salvage Rights, AI rivals on its own, session path. | Test 16 at all five settings. |\n697\t| M10 | Sound pass: music, loops, voices, mix. Polish pass: fix the worst thing seen in screenshots until no obvious one is left. | Test 14. |\n698\t| M11 | Finish (below). | Done list. |\n699\t\n700\t**If you run short, cut in this order, whole:** animals, airboat chase in C3 (make it a walk through the Reeds, keep the airboat for Salvage only if you built it), alt-plans for C2 then C5, C7's reduced form, third safe house. **Never cut:** fire, wear and jam, the held map, the rasp, buddy rescue both ways, papers, the Sill and its endings, Salvage Rights through the harness, attract, Dev mode, About.\n701\t\n702\t### Finish\n703\t\n704\t1. Pick nothing new. Remove debug prints; check no TODO, placeholder or stub text remains (grep for it).\n705\t2. Write `exit-interview.json` beside the deliverable, in exactly TASK.md's shape; validate with `python3 -m json.tool`. Suggested catalogue values: type Game, genre Shooter, source Far Cry 2, series Far Cry, players 1-4, tags `3d`, `first-person`, `vehicles`, `exploration`, `story`, `versus`. Plan field: this plan's file name. Testing Feedback comes from `test/ISSUES.md`, Engine Feedback partly from `ENGINE-CHANGES.md`.\n706\t3. Rebuild, so the About screen carries those answers (`build.mjs` inlines the JSON). Rerun the tests once on the final file.\n707\t4. Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply too, as TASK.md says. Usage: \"added on import\".\n708\t5. Delete `engine-repo/` and scratch output. Stop any server by PID.\n709\t\n710\t---\n711\t\n712\t## 16. TASK.md coverage\n713\t\n714\t| TASK.md asks for | Where |\n715\t|---|---|\n716\t| Original game inspired by the source; world, characters, themes, tone turned into mechanics and UX | 1, 3, 8, 9 |\n717\t| Genre and perspective chosen | 1 |\n718\t| Title: playful riff, chosen by real RNG | Your job, per TASK.md; header of this plan |\n719\t| Research | Done for you (engine, hub, source). Add your own if you want; report it honestly in Source Information. |\n720\t| Single HTML; dependencies | 2.2, A1 |\n721\t| Tech stack on the handoff, engine changes allowed | 2.1, 2.3, 2.4 |\n722\t| Art direction, new assets | 3, 7, 8 |\n723\t| Animation: native base, new animations | 4, 5, 8 (kit's procedural skeleton, overlay pen keyframes, no frame lists) |\n724\t| Audio in code, gibberish voices, music 10% | 12, A7 |\n725\t| Online via AI Hub, and on its own | 13 |\n726\t| Dev folder, bundle in root, no reading outside, ports and PIDs | 2.1, A8 |\n727\t| Performance unlimited, no FPS targets | Spend freely: raise `GRASS_R`, flame counts, `lights`, `glowLights`, soldiers at each post. Don't optimise. |\n728\t| Testing rules, full scripted playthrough | 14 |\n729\t| Computer constraints: stubs for pad, touch, audio, second player, phone, TV | 14, A8 |\n730\t| Feature-complete demo, polished slice, built out later with normal tools | 1 (length), 2.2 (data tables), 11 (Dev tools) |\n731\t| Dev mode from pause, tools, live sliders, reset | 11 |\n732\t| Attract mode at 10 s, looping, cheats, any input exits | 11 |\n733\t| Narrative tone | 9 |\n734\t| 10-foot, controller-first, native keyboard and mouse, hover focus, prompts, Xbox option | 4, 11, A7 |\n735\t| No dense data screens | 11 |\n736\t| Touch-only notice, settings, attract runs | 11, A7 |\n737\t| Done: no stubs | 15, Finish |\n738\t| About/Credits, chat reply, exit-interview.json | 11, 15 |\n739\t\n740\t---\n741\t\n742\t## Appendix A: verified recipes\n743\t\n744\tAll of this ran on the kit at commit `0a46310`. Adapt names; keep the logic.\n745\t\n746\t### A1. Build script and page\n747\t\n748\t```js\n749\t// build.mjs: run from the dev folder. Write the deliverable's name from TASK.md into OUT."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ea1b61d-e1b8-4350-be76-ae4a4cbc51a9","uuid":"10b10bfd-aee7-416e-8be1-f67cfba29f9a","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:14:19.556Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211923__xa49253/work/PLAN.md","content":"- Nobody explains themselves. Nobody calls you a hero. No exclamation marks except in screams.\n- Jokes are how people avoid saying the thing.\n- The narrator never appears: only letters, logbooks, radio.\n- Every line is English on screen with gibberish voice under it.\n\nWrite more lines in this voice when you need them; use these exactly where given.\n\n### Cast\n\n- **Ilse Tarn, \"the Surveyor\"**: 71, chain-smoker, the colonial water board's last hydrologist. She drew the diversion that killed the Amaranth. For nine years she has sold rifles and water rights to both armies so that neither will ever have enough men left to hold the dam. You came to kill her. She is the only honest person in the country and that is no comfort. *\"I measured this lake for thirty years. It was the only honest thing in the country and I killed it with a pencil.\"*\n- **Mr. Abel Cray**: Meridian Water Consortium's lawyer; hired you; punctual. Only appears as a letter and on the helipad.\n- **Sister Perpetua**: runs Saint Odile's, keeps a count of the living in a school exercise book. *\"I don't pray for you. I count you. It's more accurate.\"*\n- **Captain Lucan Dray**: Authority quartermaster. *\"The Authority does not kill people. The Authority reconciles accounts.\"*\n- **Colonel Dorothea Renn**: Authority commander, prim, tired. *\"A controlled burn is one we have filed the form for.\"*\n- **Comrade Teacher Joachim Sell**: Front commander, ex-schoolteacher, chalk on his sleeve. *\"Three trucks. Minus three trucks. Show your work.\"* And: *\"The Front has no prisoners. We have remainders.\"*\n- **Mr. Sunday**: arms dealer in the hold of a dry-docked trawler, cheerful as a tax refund. *\"Everything on this boat is guaranteed until it leaves this boat.\"* And: *\"You want clean hands, see the Sister. You want a clean rifle, that's eight stones.\"*\n- **Papa Static**: Radio Free Amaranth, one man and a car battery.\n\n### The radio (vehicle radio, random order; write 20 more)\n\n- \"Fish prices, Port Clement, this morning. Perch: none. Carp: none. Sturgeon: there is a man who remembers one.\"\n- \"Weather: dry. The Authority reminds you the weather is temporary. The Front reminds you the Authority is.\"\n- \"To the gentleman who keeps setting fire to the Tannery road. Your mother has asked me to say something and I told her I would not.\"\n- \"The ceasefire enters its ninth month. It has killed more people than the war. We wish it well.\"\n- \"This is the shipping forecast. There is no shipping. Good night.\"\n\n### Barks (gibberish with subtitle; write 8 per faction)\n\n- **Authority:** \"Contact. File it later.\" / \"The ceasefire is in effect! Fire!\" / \"Who authorised that?\"\n- **Front:** \"Subtract him!\" / \"Carry the two, comrade!\" / \"Burn it! Burn it all!\"\n- **Wounded:** \"Not like this. Not in triplicate.\" / \"Tell them I was at the school.\"\n- **Buddy rescuing you:** \"Up. Not dead. Not yet, anyway. You owe me a drink you'll never buy.\" / \"Stop bleeding on my boots.\"\n\n### Contracts (table `CONTRACTS`; an order the player mostly can't break)\n\nEach record: `{ id, title, giver, faction, brief: [...lines], papers, steps: [...], alt, pay, after }`. Step kinds: `goto`, `talk`, `kill`, `take`, `deliver`, `ignite`, `destroy`, `hold`, `drive`, `read`, `choice`, `script`. Each step has a `bot` hint so the playthrough bot and attract mode can do it. Current step's target drives the pencil circle and the locator.\n\n| # | Title (giver) | What happens | Teaches | Alt-plan and its twist | Pays |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| P0 | Terms of Engagement (letter) | See below. | Look, walk, fire, jam, fit | none | none |\n| P1 | Transit Papers (Sister Perpetua) | Drive the clinic jeep from Saint Odile's through G3 on the clinic's pass, give a satchel to \"the woman with one shoe\" in the Salt Shed camp. Meet Best Buddy at the Shed. Claim it. Sleep. | Map, watch, jeep, papers, bed, save | none | 2 ampoules |\n| C1 | Arrears (Dray, Authority, Kilometre Nine) | Kill the Front's paymaster at Station Four. Take his ledger back to Dray. | Monocular, tagging, night stealth, crate, first visit to Mr. Sunday | **Best Buddy:** take the cashbox under the pump too. Twist: an alarm; Best Buddy comes to help, gets pinned, goes down: your first rescue-or-mercy choice. | 6, +6 |\n| C2 | Long Division (Sell, Front, Red Steps) | Three water trucks cross the Causeway at dusk. \"Three minus three.\" Technical escort. Fire in the verge reeds is allowed. | Vehicle combat, RPG, mounted gun, patrol AI | **Second:** keep one truck. Twist: it's shot to pieces; drive it to Red Steps with black smoke, repair it under fire, and find the cargo isn't water. It's rifles. Both sides' stencils. | 8, +4 |\n| C3 | Exit Visas (Sister Perpetua) | At night, go to the hull of the *Saint Brendan* at the Fleet, take forged visas from a smuggler, then return by airboat across the Remnant and through the Reeds. A patrol's flare lights the reeds behind you. Beeper leads to a hidden case on the way. | Airboat, locator, night, outrunning fire | none | 4 ampoules (3 if `tentsBurned` or a civilian died) |\n| C4 | Fire Season (Renn, Authority, sent via Dray) | She supplies a worn Gardener (not an unlock). Burn Reed Camp from upwind. Mid-job the wind turns south-east, toward the Salt Shed camp. Sister calls: \"Whatever you lit, it's coming to us.\" You can leave it, or back-burn a strip across the mud before it arrives. The tents burn or don't (`tentsBurned`) and everyone mentions it. | Fire as a weapon, back-burning, consequence | none | 10 |\n| C5 | Remainder (Sell, Front) | Kill Colonel Renn on the Customs House steps at the treaty signing in Port Clement. Sell hands you a worn Curate for a long shot from the old harbour wall, or walk in on Authority papers with a bomb in a case. Then the town burns: scripted ignition at three points, militia both ways. Get out. Mr. Sunday moves his stock to a hulk at the Fleet. Two more posts appear. The mask keeps Port Clement black. **End of Act II.** | Sniping, papers, big fire set piece | **Third:** Third plants the bomb while you cover. Twist: Third is caught in the blast radius (rescue-or-mercy in a burning street). | 14, +6 |\n| C6 | Soundings (Tarn, by locator) | \"This is the woman you came to kill.\" Read any 3 of 8 survey stakes (below; ones already found count). Then the road to the Sill opens on the map. Finding all 8 changes one line at the end. | Collectibles that matter, exploring the scorched map | none | none |\n| C7 | The Last Reconciliation (Best Buddy) | \"Drink at the Shed. All of us. We've been talking.\" Every surviving buddy is there. \"Meridian doubled it. You'd do the same. You have done the same.\" They attack: 200 HP, good guns, they rescue each other, and the shed's perimeter is lit. If none survive, Cray's men do it instead and Best Buddy's empty chair gets one line from Sunday. | Fire, everything, and paying for pillar 4 | none | their stones |\n| F | The Sill | Canyon road, both armies climbing it, fire behind you. Top of the dam: the control house. Tarn, dying in a chair. | Everything | none | endings |\n\n**P0, opening (your hands bound, in first person):**\n1. Black. A typed letter on screen with voice: \"Terms of engagement. You will locate and remove the engineer I. Tarn. Fee on completion: two hundred stones. Meridian Water Consortium regrets it cannot be reached. A. Cray.\"\n2. You sit in the bed of a Front pickup at dusk on the ring road, wrists tied, a boy with a rifle opposite, radio playing fish prices. Look around only.\n3. A Provisional gun truck ambushes it. The truck rolls. You crawl out with wrists cut free. The boy, dying, shoves a rusty Verger at you.\n4. The grass is alight and the wind is on your back. Prompt, in the writing: *Run into the black.* Run through the flame line onto burnt ground.\n5. Two soldiers. The Verger jams on the second shot. Clear prompt.\n6. Your first fit comes as you win. You go down.\n7. Wake on a cot at Saint Odile's in the morning, Sister Perpetua over you: \"You were on the road when the grass went. That makes you lucky or stupid, and you don't look lucky.\" / \"That cough is the seabed. It doesn't leave. These will hold it off. There are never enough of these.\" / \"Take the jeep to the Salt Shed. Give the satchel to the woman with one shoe. Bring back the jeep, if it's still a jeep.\"\n\n**Briefs to use:**\n- **Dray (C1):** \"A man at Station Four collects a water levy on water that isn't there. Close his account. Bring me his ledger.\" / \"You'll be paid on completion, less handling.\"\n- **Best Buddy's call (C1):** \"You're doing Dray's man at Four? He keeps a cashbox under the pump. Nothing will go wrong. I said that out loud, didn't I.\"\n- **Sell (C2):** \"Sit. We'll do this the way I did it with the eight-year-olds.\" / \"Three water trucks come over the Causeway at dusk. Three minus three.\" / \"Show your work.\"\n- **Sister (C3):** \"There's a man in the hull of the *Saint Brendan* who forges exit visas. I don't ask how he eats.\" / \"Go at night. Come back across the Reeds. The posts can't see through reeds, and neither can God.\"\n- **Renn (C4):** \"The Front keeps a camp in the Reeds. The wind is out of the west until noon. I have it in writing.\" / \"There are some tents downwind. They've been notified.\" (They haven't.)\n- **Sell (C5):** \"Colonel Renn signs the water treaty on the Customs House steps on Thursday. She has a very good pen.\" / \"Take away the pen. Take away the hand.\" / \"The remainder is yours to keep.\"\n- **Sunday after C5:** \"Port Clement is closed for stocktaking.\"\n- **Tarn (C6):** \"This is the woman you came to kill. I've had your passport for a week. You have a bad photograph and one lung.\" / \"I left my readings in the basin, stake by stake. Read three. Then come up to the Sill and tell me I'm wrong.\"\n\n### The Soundings (eight survey stakes across the basin, each a tin box on a tripod)\n\nPicking one up raises a logbook page in your hands (like the map; you can still be shot) and plays Tarn's voice. Place them so that finding them means seeing the whole map, including one deep in the Reeds and one in the *Saint Brendan*.\n\n1. \"1958, Station A. Forty-one metres. We came in on the spring tide with the Minister's wife on deck, and she asked me if it had a bottom. I said, madam, everything does.\"\n2. \"1963. Thirty-eight metres. The cotton scheme took the river this year. They gave me a medal. Water doesn't read the citation.\"\n3. \"1971. Twenty-six. The fishermen have started tying their boats longer. Nobody has told them why. I was asked not to.\"\n4. \"1979. Eleven. Port Clement's quay now ends in mud at low water. The Harbourmaster asked whether I could do something. I told him I already had.\"\n5. \"1986. Four. The fleet sat down on the bottom this winter, one hull at a time. It was very quiet. You could hear the radios still playing the fish prices.\"\n6. \"1991. Zero. I walked to Station A with the lead line anyway. I stood on the place I'd measured and dropped the lead on my foot. That's a joke. Write it down.\"\n7. \"1998. The dust. They call it the rasp. My own lungs are at eleven metres and falling.\"\n8. \"Last sounding. I have sold rifles to both sides for nine years so neither will have men left to hold the Sill. When it is unguarded someone will open it. If you are reading this, it's you. I'm sorry. No. I'm not. Bring your own pencil.\"\n\n### The Sill and the endings\n\nTarn in the control house, a cigarette she can't lift: \"Forty-one metres. That's what it was. There's a wheel behind me. It wants two hands, and I have a bad heart and a worse character.\" / \"The Sister's column is on the Causeway. It needs six minutes. Both armies are coming up the road. You might manage one of those.\" / \"Or there's Mr. Cray's helicopter. He's very punctual.\" Then a choice of three.\n\nThe flood is one water plane (A5) rising over the basin. Hold it low until the gates open. Then let the plane climb from below the seabed to the Causeway's height in about 90 s. Cells under water turn wet with steam where they were burning, so fire and water meet in front of you. From the dam top you can see the whole country go. It costs almost nothing and it's the best shot in the game. Build it well.\n\n- **The Contract** (take the helicopter): Cray hands you the stones, and you fly out, first person, over the burn scars. \"Cray pays in full. From the air the grass is still burning in the shape of your route.\" Radio: \"Fish prices, Port Clement. None. None. None.\"\n- **The Arithmetic** (open now): both hands on the wheel, hold R2 + L2 (both mouse buttons). \"The water goes through the Causeway at eleven minutes past. The Authority's column goes under, and the Front's, and the other one. Sister Perpetua's count stops at four hundred and six. You stay on the wheel. Somebody should have done the sum.\"\n- **The Sounding** (hold six minutes, then open): a timed defence of the dam top against both armies, with the canyon burning and a fit waiting for you. The radio counts the column across, in Papa Static's voice. Then the wheel. Water rises to the control house window and the picture goes white. \"Six minutes. Then the wheel. The column clears the east shore with nineteen seconds left. Nobody ever finds out who held it.\" Then one typed line, alone: \"Station A. Forty-one metres.\"\n\nFinding all 8 Soundings adds Tarn's last words before the choice: \"You read them all. Nobody reads them all. Then you know what it's for.\"\n\nCredits roll over the water. Then return to the title. A finished save offers \"New Game\" and, on Continue, lets you replay from the Sill.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Money, safe houses, saves\n\n- **Stones** (uncut diamonds) are the only money. Pay comes from contracts. 12 hidden cases hold 2-5 stones each: on hulks, in the Reeds, at wrecks, in a burnt farm. The locator finds them. Bodies don't carry stones.\n- **Mr. Sunday's boat:** a visit is a big, simple screen (section 11): his catalogue, one gun at a time. Buying unlocks that gun at every crate. He sells guns and throwables, nothing else.\n- **Safe houses** (Salt Shed, the Lamp, the Tannery, the Water Tower): hostile until cleared or claimed; each has a bed, a weapon crate, a buddy's chair. **Bed:** watch dial on screen, pick an hour with the stick or mouse (the dial is big), sleep: fade, time jumps, posts may refill, ash regrows a little, blood cleans off the gloves, autosave. Fits can't happen in bed.\n- **Saves:** `game.saves` with `menu: { saves: { version: 1, ... } }`. `saves.canSave` is true only near a bed. Autosave on sleep and on contract completion. The title's Continue uses `saves.latest()`. Save data: player, inventory with each gun's `cond`, ampoules, stones, flags, contract state, buddy states, post states, `lung`, hour, wind, Soundings found, and the burn mask (RLE, base64). No saves in a hub session.\n\n---\n\n## 11. Screens and 10-foot UX\n\n**Rules from TASK.md.** Designed for a DualSense on a TV at ten feet; keyboard and mouse feel native on the same screens. No dense web-style screens: at most 6 rows or one big card at a time. Prompts follow the last device. PlayStation glyphs by default, an Xbox option in Settings (A7, VERIFIED). Mouse hover moves focus and click picks, on every menu; release pointer lock when one opens (`document.exitPointerLock()`) and capture again on the next click. In the world, the mouse aims and fires; on things your hands hold (map, logbook, Sunday's card, the watch dial), left click acts on what's under the pencil or cursor.\n\n**HUD (`r.overlay` in the kit's pixel font at `res: 'ps1', expand: true`):** at 1080p one game pixel is 4.5 screen pixels, so scale 1 text is 31 px tall and reads from the couch. Show almost nothing:\n- Bottom left: 5 health segments, syrette count as small tubes.\n- Bottom right: ammo count and gun name, fading after 3 s of no shooting; the condition mark below .4.\n- Centre: a small dot, not a big crosshair. It grows a little with spread.\n- Damage arrows at the screen's edge (the kit's `hitDirs`). Red and white veils for damage and fits.\n- Bottom centre: one context prompt at a time: glyph chip + verb (\"□ Repair\", \"E Sleep\").\n- Lower third: subtitles with coloured speaker names (`E.Dialog`, `{ modal: false, auto }` for radio).\n- A new objective shows as one line for 4 s. After that it's only on the map.\n\nNo compass, minimap, ammo bars or kill feed. In first play, teach each control once when first needed, using the same chip prompts.\n\n**Title screen.** The one world, fixed camera, dusk, at the edge of a slow grass fire with the Lamp's beam in the distance. Game title in `E.font.title`, then `E.Menu`: Continue, New Game, Salvage Rights (section 13), Settings, About. After **10 s without input** start attract mode.\n\n**Merc select.** Four passports laid out; one big at a time, left and right to browse, hover to focus. Photo (draw a head close-up with the pen on an overlay or a `Humanoid` `drawPortrait`), name, one line, one perk. Confirm stamps it.\n\n**Mr. Sunday's catalogue, watch dial, logbook page, contract brief:** each a single large card. Gun cards show the first-person gun model turning on the overlay pen, name, Sunday's one-line patter, cost. Left and right to browse, ✕ or click to buy.\n\n**Pause menu.** Use the engine's: Resume, Dev mode, About, Save (near a bed), Load, Settings, Controls, Full screen, Quit to title. `menu: { items: [['Dev mode', fn], ['About', fn]], settings, controls, saves }`. VERIFIED: these appear and click correctly. Add the CSS in A7 so it's TV-sized. In a hub session: `quit: false`, no Dev, no saves.\n\n**Dev mode (TASK.md: reachable from pause, standard tools, live sliders, reset).** A panel of your own drawn with the pixel font, world running under it so sliders show their effect at once. D-pad or mouse to select, left/right or drag to adjust, ✕ or click to toggle. Three tabs of at most 8 rows.\n\n- **Balance (live sliders, with Reset to defaults):** `fireSpread`, `wind`, `wear`, `jam`, `enemyAccuracy`, `enemyDamage`, `enemySight`, `playerDamage`, `lung`, `rescueChance`, `postRespawn`, `carTop`, `dayLength`. All read from one `TUNE` table next to `TUNE_DEFAULTS`.\n- **Cheats:** god mode, infinite ammo, no clip, no fits, no jams, freeze AI, reveal map, all guns, +50 stones, refill.\n- **World:** teleport to any site, skip to contract N, complete objective, set hour, set wind, start dust storm, ignite here, spawn squad, force a fit, force a rescue, force a jam, flood level, show fire cells, show AI state labels, show frame stats (`world.stats`), log player position to console. That last one is the level designer's tool: pair it with the `SITES` table.\n\n**About / Credits (from pause and title).** Big text in the engine's HTML shell: `const ui = new E.Shell(game, {})` keeps the standard menu, and `ui.show('help', { sections: [[heading, text], ...] })` shows it (VERIFIED with CSS zoom, mouse click and long text). Contents exactly as TASK.md lists: Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback, plus library credits (my-3D2dge MIT, three.js r182 MIT, Rapier 0.19.3 Apache-2.0, any CC0 store props used). Fill it from `exit-interview.json` via `window.__answers` (A1), so the two can't disagree. See section 15 for ordering. **Trap:** the Shell focuses Back, which scrolls the panel (`.esh-mod`) to the bottom. Set its `scrollTop = 0` after opening, and each step move `scrollTop` from the sticks and d-pad, so a controller can read the whole thing. Test it.\n\n**Attract mode (TASK.md).** After 10 s idle on the title, a looping AI-played demo in the real game, using the one world, cheats freely, saving nothing. It's the `Bot` (section 14) running a fixed reel of 8 vignettes, 10-15 s each, teleporting between them with a dither cut:\n1. Jeep at dusk along the Causeway past the Fleet, radio subtitles.\n2. Monocular sweep over a guard post, tagging.\n3. Firefight, the gun jams, it's cleared.\n4. Gardener lights the grass, wind takes it, soldiers run burning.\n5. Map in hand, locator beeping, a case found.\n6. Going down, buddy drags you out, surgery.\n7. Airboat through burning reeds at night.\n8. Dawn at the Lamp, the flood for a moment, title card.\n\nA small \"DEMO\" tag and the prompt to press anything. Music at its normal setting. **Any input** (key, mouse move or click, pad button or stick, touch) returns to the title at once with state reset. Then the idle clock restarts, and the demo loops forever until then.\n\n**Touch-only devices (TASK.md).** `new E.Game({ touch: 'never' })`. VERIFIED: phones show \"Controller or keyboard required\" with a Settings button. No touch controls. The notice's opaque backdrop would hide the attract mode: use the CSS in A7. Attract mode must start and loop there too: the idle clock doesn't need input.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Sound (all generated; no audio files)\n\n**Settings:** music defaults to 10% (`{ key: 'music', value: .1 }`, VERIFIED: `audio.musicVolume` reads .1 after boot).\n\n**Music** (original; the engine's song format, `audio.music(song, { fade })`, with `layer` for intensity). Spare, dry, sun-struck. Plucked low strings over a drone, hand drums, long silences; nothing heroic.\n- Build a plucked-string voice: render Karplus-Strong once into an `AudioBuffer` at boot (plain JS loop, no files), and play it on `audio.bus('music')` at varying `playbackRate`, scheduled from `audio.onBeat` or `audio.pos`.\n- **Themes:** Title \"Dry Season\" (slow 6/8, D minor pentatonic: `D3 - - A3 - - C4 - - D4 - - | F4 - D4 - C4 - A3 - - - - -`, extend it); Explore (mostly silent: a phrase every 40-90 s, different by hour); Tension (a drone and a heartbeat drum when soldiers are alerted); Combat (hand drums and a bass ostinato, layered in and out with alert level); Fire (a rising metallic drone tied to distance from the front); Finale (all of it, and then nothing).\n\n**Effects.** Start from the kit's `SOUNDS`. Add a distinct gunshot per weapon (layered noise and sub thump, with a delayed quiet echo by distance), jam clunk, rack, syrette hiss, pliers squelch, knife, lighter flick, finger snap, map rustle, locator beep, watch tick, bottle smash, flare pop, flamethrower roar, tank hiss, machete, cough set (at least 4), breath catch, footsteps per biome (salt crunch, ash whisper, reed rustle, boardwalk).\n\n**Loops** (your own nodes on `audio.bus('sfx')`, with gain and `StereoPanner`): engine (saw and noise, rate from speed, a stutter when damaged), airboat fan, fire crackle and roar, wind by strength, cicadas at dusk, night insects, far-off gunfire now and then, helicopter. Sound position is manual: gain from distance, pan from bearing.\n\n**Voices (Animalese/Simlish style).** `new E.Dialog(game, { voice: (ch, i, talk) => babble(ch, talk.name) })` (the engine calls this per letter).\n- `babble`: a saw at the speaker's f0 (with a tiny wobble) through two bandpass filters set by the letter's vowel class, a 60-90 ms envelope; consonants add a 12 ms noise tick. Connect to `audio.bus('voice')`.\n- Per-speaker table: f0, rate, formant shift: Tarn low and slow with a rasp of noise, Sister flat and quick, Sell precise, Sunday bright, Dray nasal.\n- Radio voices (Papa Static, buddies' calls) add a 600-2400 Hz band filter and light clipping. Soldier barks use the same voice on short nonsense.\n- Everyone speaks gibberish. Everything is subtitled.\n\nRumble: `input.rumble` on shots, blasts, fits and crashes.\n\n---\n\n## 13. Multiplayer: \"Salvage Rights\"\n\nFollow the AI Hub Session Protocol v1 (`https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub`, the README's content is your contract). The hub runs lobby, seats, network, clock and scoreboard. You write the round.\n\n**Mode:** `shared-world`, 1-4 players, about 6 minutes.\n\n```html\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"6\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Bank the most diamonds before the fire takes the Fleet\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Stick or WASD move, R2 or click fire, L2 or right click aim, Square or E use\">\n```\n\n**The round.**\n- Dusk. Play area: a circle r = 400 m around (980, 1320): Reed Camp, the Remnant, the Fleet, the Salt Shed.\n- Every merc drops at a seeded spot with a Verger and a machete, around 12 diamond cases (seeded spots: hulks, tents, wrecks), with locators on, and Front militia in hulks and tents. Worn guns lie around (they jam like everyone's). Two pickups and an airboat.\n- At 0:30 the upwind edge is lit in three places with wind toward the centre and `fireSpread` ×1.6, so the front crosses the area in about 5.5 minutes.\n- Carry stones to the **Ferryman's truck** at the Salt Shed (on the salt, which doesn't burn). Hold use 3 s to bank.\n- If you die: 8 s out, respawn at a safe spot, your carried stones stay on the ground as a case. No buddy rescue here. Players can shoot each other.\n- Ends at 6:00 or `time-up`. The host calls `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, stats, awards })`, ranked by stones banked. Awards: *Arsonist* (most cells lit), *Last Clean Gun* (fewest jams), *Harbourmaster* (most stones).\n\n**On its own (outside a hub):** `AIHub.connect` is not called, `AIHub.active` is false, and the game plays exactly as designed. Salvage Rights is on the title menu with three AI mercs as rivals (soldier AI with goals: nearest case, then the truck; flee fire; shoot whoever's close), through the same code with a no-op network layer. So the mode exists both ways. (Stretch: `game.splitScreen(2)` on one screen for a second local pad, using `world.addCamera`.)\n\n**Architecture.** The host's copy runs AI, fire, cases and the score. It's the same sim as single player with `players[]` instead of one hero. Every copy builds the same terrain and structures from constants.\n\nKeep it simple and it will feel lag-free:\n\n| Direction | Message | Reliable | Rate |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| client → host | `{t:'i', x,y,z, yw,pt, a}`: own feet (ints), look (×1000), action bits, vehicle id | no | 15/s |\n| client → host | `{t:'f', w, o:[x,y,z], d:[dx,dy,dz], n}`: shots merged | yes | ≤4/s |\n| client → host | `{t:'u', id}` use; `{t:'ig', x,y,r}` ignite request | yes | on event |\n| host → all | `{t:'s', at, P:[...], E:[...], V:[...]}`: snapshot, flat int arrays, soldiers within 300 m of any player, keep under 1,100 bytes (split by kind if not) | no | 12/s |\n| host → all | `{t:'e', L:[...]}`: batched events: tracers, impacts, damage to you, deaths, pickups, bank, newly lit cells | yes | 4/s |\n\n- Staying under 20 messages a second per copy is your job: the client silently drops the rest.\n- **Own movement is client-authoritative** (no anti-cheat is asked for, and it means no input lag). The host mirrors each client's hero with `place` so rays hit it. A driven vehicle's owner simulates it and reports it; the host owns unoccupied ones.\n- **The host casts all shots** with `world.ray` and applies damage. A client shows its own flash and tracer at once.\n- **Fire on clients:** apply lit cells from events; burn-out and flames run locally. Cells are just `(index)` and a client-side timer.\n- **Interpolate** others 100 ms behind using `at`. Clients draw soldiers from snapshots: `e.a` can be a plain object, since `syncRaider` only reads it.\n- **Names and colours** come from the hub: name tags with `world.project` and `E.font.text` (canvas, never HTML), an armband in seat colour (`LOOKS.accent`).\n- **Time** in a round is `AIHub.time()`, not game time. Before 0 show a big 3-2-1 and hold players still. The kit's frame cap slows game time on slow machines but must not extend the round.\n- **`leave`:** remove that hero and drop their stones. **`end`:** `game.stop()`, mute, ignore input.\n- **`AIHub.server`** (a host with no player): VERIFIED by replacing the scene's `draw` with a no-op. No hero, no camera, no input.\n- In a session: no title, menus or attract; `live: true`, `autoPause: false`, `quit: false`; no saves. Storage is memory.\n- Don't declare `hub:webgpu`; the game runs on either backend. If World3D can't start at all in a session, call `AIHub.fail(message)`.\n- Standard card: the hub's. (Stretch: `card: true` with your own card; it must obey the README's \"The card\" section, including Enter = Ready.)\n\n**The boot order is the trap (VERIFIED).** The harness waits at most 20 s for every copy's `ready()`, and it runs up to 4 copies on one main thread. The kit's full boot, with `ready()` after the title stage and shader warm-up, took **20.8 s and failed** at 4 players. With `connect()` in an inline script straight after the client, no title world, and `ready()` before the warm-up, **all scenarios passed**: 1, 2 and 4 players, `host-leave`, `server`, at 150 ms latency, 50 jitter, 5% loss. Appendix A1 and A6, followed literally on the kit, passed all five harness runs. Keep that order as your boot grows, and test it (section 14). Keep `planLand` and world build under about 1 s per copy; anything heavier goes after `ready()`.\n\n---\n\n## 14. Testing\n\nTASK.md's rules: one command, prints only failures and a one-line count, rerun only after changing what it covers, screenshots only for what a script can't check, no subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit. Keep a tally of issues caught in `test/ISSUES.md`: the exit interview asks for the numbers.\n\n**Command:** `python3 test/run.py` (system Python has Playwright 1.63; no `playwright install`; keep one or two browsers open; \"Target closed\" means memory ran out, not a bug).\n\n**The fast rig (VERIFIED).** Open the built file from `file://` with `?norender=1`, which boots `W3.init(game, { render: false })`. It boots in .45 s with no GPU work, and `game.advance(60)` runs 60 game seconds in 1.4 s, about 44× real time, with the same `world.hash()` as with a renderer. Call `game.stop()` first so only your `advance` steps run. Scripted input works: `game.input.hold('up')`, `game.input.tap('fire')`, `hold('up', false)`. Everything else about the world works without a renderer (rays, ground, vehicles). Expose `game.debug = { snapshot(), teleport(x, y, z) }`, plus `window.__game` with `S`, `world`, `Fire`, `Contracts`, `Dev`, `Bot`.\n\n**Tests to have (each a small in-page function returning problems):**\n1. Boot, no errors, title shows, music setting .1, glyphs `playstation`.\n2. Replay proof: same `run(n)` hash twice.\n3. Fire: spreads faster downwind than upwind, stops at road and salt, ash doesn't re-ignite, a burning actor takes damage, mask values change; save and load round-trips the mask.\n4. Wear: `cond` falls per shot, jam happens at low `cond` under a fixed seed, clear works, break empties the slot.\n5. Health and surgery: segments refill only to the top; syrette; surgery at the last segment; rasp fit at 100; ampoule ends it; second fit without one blacks out.\n6. Vehicles: enter, exit, drive to speed on road, slower on mud, crash damage, stall under 20%, repair, wreck burns.\n7. Papers: a post waves you through with papers; burns them when you fire; hostile without.\n8. Buddies: rescue fires at 0 HP; cooldown; buddy down, syrette; buddy down, mercy; dead stays dead through save and load.\n9. Contracts: every contract's steps complete under `Bot`; `tentsBurned` and the other flags reach their lines.\n10. **Scripted playthrough of the whole game:** `Bot.playthrough()` from New Game through all contracts and each of the three endings, with god mode and teleports allowed between sites but real input to act: aim and fire, throw, drive short legs, use. Asserts each contract's completion and each ending. Keep under about 3 minutes.\n11. Attract: starts at 10 s idle, shows at least 8 vignettes, loops; each of key, mouse, pad button and stick exits it; save data untouched.\n12. Input: the stub gamepad in A8 reads `R2`; a key press flips prompts to keys; a mouse move to `Left click`; Settings Xbox flips to `RT`.\n13. Dev mode: every slider changes its `TUNE` value and the effect; Reset restores defaults; every cheat toggles.\n14. Audio: build one `OfflineAudioContext` render of the babble and one gunshot: non-silent, no NaN. `AnalyserNode` on the music bus at default is quieter than effects.\n15. Phone (Playwright `iPhone 13` profile): the notice shows, Settings opens, no touch buttons, attract runs.\n16. **Hub (A8):** copy the build to `hub/game.html`, serve `hub/` on a port the OS picks, and run `harness.html?game=game.html&players=N&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&scenario=S&play=8000` for (1, standard), (2, standard), (4, standard), (4, host-leave), (2, server). Pass when `window.__hubCheck.pass`. Stop the server by its PID. Also play a real two-page round through the harness once with `render` on, and check both see each other's stones.\n17. WebGPU smoke once at the end: Appendix A9's flags and stand-in canvas. No page errors, `My3D2dge.World3D.backend === 'WebGPU'`, same replay hash as WebGL 2.\n\n**Screenshots** at 1920×1080 with the renderer on, only for what scripts can't judge: title, noon, dusk, night, fire front, ash, held map, a soldier's face at 2 m, a jeep, a hulk, the Lamp at night, Sunday's card, pause, Dev panel, the flood. Run at about 4.5 fps here, so set state, wait for a few frames, shoot. Fix what looks wrong; don't re-shoot what hasn't changed.\n\n---\n\n## 15. Build order\n\nWork in order. Each milestone ends with the game running and the test command passing. Don't start the next with the last one broken.\n\n| # | Milestone | Done when |\n|---|---|---|\n| M0 | Setup: pieces, `build.mjs`, the kit running from `file://` as one file, `test/run.py` with tests 1-2, fast rig. | One-file build boots; `?norender=1` hash stable. |\n| M1 | Land: bowl terrain, biomes, sites, roads, scatter, hulks, the Lamp, the Sill. Time of day, wind. Remove kit HUD clutter. | Walk and fly (no clip) the whole map; screenshots at noon, dusk, night. |\n| M2 | Player: remove shields, slide, zip, climb, third person. New controls. Health and syrette. Weapons table, wear, jam, break. Machete, throwables. | Tests 4, 5 (part). |\n| M3 | **Fire (the signature, get it right first):** cells, mask, flames, smoke, spread, igniters, actors, AI flight, sound. | Test 3; the fire screenshots look dangerous. |\n| M4 | Hands: map, locator, monocular, surgery, rasp, repair; dash and steering hands. | Test 5; each tool raises, works and lowers with a sound. |\n| M5 | Vehicles: jeep, technical, truck, airboat, seat, damage, repair, convoys, radio. | Test 6. |\n| M6 | People: looks and faces, barks, wounded, flanking, posts and papers, civilians. Buddies: rescue both ways, permadeath. | Tests 7, 8. |\n| M7 | Story: contract runner, every contract and text, alt-plans, Soundings, saves, safe houses, Sunday, endings, flood. | Tests 9, 10. A full play by bot. |\n| M8 | Screens: title, merc select, HUD pass, pause items, TV CSS, Dev mode, About, attract, phone notice. | Tests 11, 12, 13, 15. |\n| M9 | Multiplayer: net layer, `players[]`, Salvage Rights, AI rivals on its own, session path. | Test 16 at all five settings. |\n| M10 | Sound pass: music, loops, voices, mix. Polish pass: fix the worst thing seen in screenshots until no obvious one is left. | Test 14. |\n| M11 | Finish (below). | Done list. |\n\n**If you run short, cut in this order, whole:** animals, airboat chase in C3 (make it a walk through the Reeds, keep the airboat for Salvage only if you built it), alt-plans for C2 then C5, C7's reduced form, third safe house. **Never cut:** fire, wear and jam, the held map, the rasp, buddy rescue both ways, papers, the Sill and its endings, Salvage Rights through the harness, attract, Dev mode, About.\n\n### Finish\n\n1. Pick nothing new. Remove debug prints; check no TODO, placeholder or stub text remains (grep for it).\n2. Write `exit-interview.json` beside the deliverable, in exactly TASK.md's shape; validate with `python3 -m json.tool`. Suggested catalogue values: type Game, genre Shooter, source Far Cry 2, series Far Cry, players 1-4, tags `3d`, `first-person`, `vehicles`, `exploration`, `story`, `versus`. Plan field: this plan's file name. Testing Feedback comes from `test/ISSUES.md`, Engine Feedback partly from `ENGINE-CHANGES.md`.\n3. Rebuild, so the About screen carries those answers (`build.mjs` inlines the JSON). Rerun the tests once on the final file.\n4. Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply too, as TASK.md says. Usage: \"added on import\".\n5. Delete `engine-repo/` and scratch output. Stop any server by PID.\n\n---\n\n## 16. TASK.md coverage\n\n| TASK.md asks for | Where |\n|---|---|\n| Original game inspired by the source; world, characters, themes, tone turned into mechanics and UX | 1, 3, 8, 9 |\n| Genre and perspective chosen | 1 |\n| Title: playful riff, chosen by real RNG | Your job, per TASK.md; header of this plan |\n| Research | Done for you (engine, hub, source). Add your own if you want; report it honestly in Source Information. |\n| Single HTML; dependencies | 2.2, A1 |\n| Tech stack on the handoff, engine changes allowed | 2.1, 2.3, 2.4 |\n| Art direction, new assets | 3, 7, 8 |\n| Animation: native base, new animations | 4, 5, 8 (kit's procedural skeleton, overlay pen keyframes, no frame lists) |\n| Audio in code, gibberish voices, music 10% | 12, A7 |\n| Online via AI Hub, and on its own | 13 |\n| Dev folder, bundle in root, no reading outside, ports and PIDs | 2.1, A8 |\n| Performance unlimited, no FPS targets | Spend freely: raise `GRASS_R`, flame counts, `lights`, `glowLights`, soldiers at each post. Don't optimise. |\n| Testing rules, full scripted playthrough | 14 |\n| Computer constraints: stubs for pad, touch, audio, second player, phone, TV | 14, A8 |\n| Feature-complete demo, polished slice, built out later with normal tools | 1 (length), 2.2 (data tables), 11 (Dev tools) |\n| Dev mode from pause, tools, live sliders, reset | 11 |\n| Attract mode at 10 s, looping, cheats, any input exits | 11 |\n| Narrative tone | 9 |\n| 10-foot, controller-first, native keyboard and mouse, hover focus, prompts, Xbox option | 4, 11, A7 |\n| No dense data screens | 11 |\n| Touch-only notice, settings, attract runs | 11, A7 |\n| Done: no stubs | 15, Finish |\n| About/Credits, chat reply, exit-interview.json | 11, 15 |\n\n---\n\n## Appendix A: verified recipes\n\nAll of this ran on the kit at commit `0a46310`. Adapt names; keep the logic.\n\n### A1. Build script and page\n\n```js\n// build.mjs: run from the dev folder. Write the deliverable's name from TASK.md into OUT.","numLines":330,"startLine":420,"totalLines":952}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012r9N2vHTNFK93Vz4scTgq9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
